values ('mathematics','source-scheme-draft-v2','original-v3','[{"id":"p2-q1-v3::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"46/3","solution":"(3 1/2 + 2 1/4) = 7/2 + 9/4 = 14/4 + 9/4 = 23/4. (7/8 - 1/2) = 7/8 - 1/2 = 7/8 - 4/8 = 3/8. Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal, so 23/4 ÷ 3/8 = 23/4 × 8/3 = 46/3. As a mixed number this is 15 1/3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v3::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v3::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"900.00","solution":"Deposit = 25% of 3,600 = $900.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v3::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v3::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4200.00","solution":"Instalments = 15 × 220 = $3,300. Hire purchase price = 900.00 + 3,300 = $4200.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v3::b3","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v3::b3","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"16.67","solution":"Extra paid = 4200.00 - 3,600 = $600.00. As a percentage of the cash price this is (600.00 ÷ 3,600) × 100 = 16.67%.","criteria":[]}},{"id":"p2-q1-v3::c","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"The hire purchase price is larger than the cash price, so the same difference is a smaller fraction of it","solution":"The difference between the two prices does not change. Expressing it as a percentage divides that difference by the price chosen as the base. The hire purchase price is the larger of the two, so dividing by it gives a smaller percentage.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","code":"B1","marks":1,"field":"answer","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"says the base of the percentage is larger, so the percentage is smaller","check":{"type":"prose","key":"the hire purchase price is larger, so the same difference is a smaller percentage of it","tokens":["larger","bigger","smaller","difference","same"],"mustHave":[],"forbid":[],"polarity":"positive","quorum":0.25}}]}},{"id":"p2-q2-v3::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3x^3y","solution":"Multiply the numerator: 24x^6y^5. Dividing, subtract the indices: 3x^3y.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v3::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v3::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5(m - 3n)(m + 3n)","solution":"Take out the common factor 5: 5(m^2 - 9n^2). The bracket is a difference of two squares, so the answer is 5(m - 3n)(m + 3n).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v3::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v3::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(5x - 7)(x + 2)","solution":"Split the middle term using 10 and 7: 5x^2 + 10x - 7x - 14 = 5x(x + 2) - 7(x + 2) = (5x - 7)(x + 2).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v3::c1","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v3::c1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10w + 6","solution":"Length = 4w + 3. Perimeter = 2[w + (4w + 3)] = 10w + 6.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v3::c2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v3::c2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"width 5 cm, length 23 cm","solution":"10w + 6 = 56, so 10w = 50 and w = 5. Width = 5 cm and length = 4(5) + 3 = 23 cm.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v3::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"A reflection in the x-axis (y = 0)","solution":"Each vertex keeps one coordinate and the other changes sign: (1, 2) maps to (1, -2), (4, 2) to (4, -2) and (1, 6) to (1, -6). That is a reflection in the x-axis.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v3::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v3::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(-4, 1); (-1, 1); (-4, 5)","solution":"Add the translation vector to each vertex: (1, 2) + (-5, -1) = (-4, 1); (4, 2) + (-5, -1) = (-1, 1); (1, 6) + (-5, -1) = (-4, 5).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v3::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5.00","solution":"Length = sqrt[(1 - 4)^2 + (6 - 2)^2] = sqrt(25) = 5.00 units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v3::a1","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v3::a1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"11","solution":"f(2) = 4(2) + 3 = 11.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v3::a2","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v3::a2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"59","solution":"Apply g first: g(4) = 4^2 - 2 = 14. Then f(14) = 4(14) + 3 = 59.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v3::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v3::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(x - 3)/4","solution":"Let y = 4x + 3. Interchanging the variables, x = 4y + 3, so 4y = x - 3 and y = (x - 3)/4. Check: f^-1(f(1)) = 1.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v3::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"6 and -6","solution":"x^2 - 2 = 34, so x^2 = 36 and x = +/-6. The two values are 6 and -6.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v3::a","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"11 - 15","solution":"The class 11 - 15 has the highest frequency, 16.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v3::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v3::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"13","solution":"Use the class midpoints 3, 8, 13, 18, 23. Sum of fx = 3(3) + 6(8) + 16(13) + 6(18) + 3(23) = 442. Mean = 442 / 34 = 13 kg.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v3::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3, 9, 25, 31, 34","solution":"Add the frequencies in order: 3, 9, 25, 31, 34.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v3::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v3::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"9/34","solution":"9 of the 34 parcels have a mass greater than 15 kg, so the probability is 9/34.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v3::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"346.5","solution":"Area = πr^2 = (22/7)(10.5)^2 = 346.5 m^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v3::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v3::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"2772","solution":"Volume = πr^2h = 346.5 × 8 = 2772 m^3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v3::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"528","solution":"Curved surface area = 2πrh = 2 × (22/7) × 10.5 × 8 = 528 m^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v3::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v3::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"36","solution":"Time = volume / rate = 2772 / 77 = 36 hours.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v3::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"16, 16, 32","solution":"Design 4 has a 4 by 4 block, so 16 shaded tiles, and 4 unshaded tiles against each of the 4 sides, so 16 unshaded. The total is 32.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v3::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v3::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"shaded n^2; unshaded 4n; total n^2 + 4n","solution":"The shaded tiles form an n by n block, so there are n^2 of them. There are n unshaded tiles against each of the four sides, so 4n of them. The total is n^2 + 4n, which can also be written n(n + 4). Check with n = 3: 9 + 12 = 21, which matches the table.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v3::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"16","solution":"n^2 + 4n = 320, so n^2 + 4n - 320 = 0. Factorising gives (n + 20)(n - 16) = 0, so n = 16, since a design number must be positive. Check: 16^2 + 4(16) = 320.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v3::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v3::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"80","solution":"n^2 = 400, so n = 20. The number of unshaded tiles is 4n = 4(20) = 80.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v3::a","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(x - 4)^2 - 7","solution":"Take out the factor 1 from the first two terms: 1(x^2 - 8x) + 9. Completing the square inside the bracket, x^2 - 8x = (x - 4)^2 - 16. So f(x) = (x - 4)^2 - 7.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v3::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v3::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-7","solution":"1(x - 4)^2 is never negative and is zero when x = 4, so the least value of f(x) is -7.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v3::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v3::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4","solution":"The square is zero when x - 4 = 0, that is x = 4.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v3::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = 4","solution":"The graph is symmetrical about the vertical line through the turning point, so the axis of symmetry is x = 4.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v3::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v3::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(0, 9)","solution":"When x = 0, f(0) = 9, so the graph cuts the y-axis at (0, 9).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v3::a","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"13.5","solution":"By the cosine rule, KM^2 = 9^2 + 14^2 - 2(9)(14)cos 68° = 182.60, so KM = 13.51 = 13.5 cm.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v3::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v3::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"74","solution":"Use the cosine rule again, so that an obtuse angle is found correctly: cos(LKM) = (9^2 + 13.51^2 - 14^2) / (2 × 9 × 13.51), giving angle LKM = 73.9°, which is 74° to the nearest degree. Check: the three angles 68, 73.9 and 38.1 add to 180.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v3::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"58.4","solution":"Area = 1/2 × LK × LM × sin(KLM) = 1/2 × 9 × 14 × sin 68° = 58.41 = 58.4 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v3::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"[[11, 9], [9, 15]]","solution":"Pair each row of M with each column of N: entry (1,1) = 4(2) + 3(1) = 11; entry (1,2) = 4(0) + 3(3) = 9; entry (2,1) = 2(2) + 5(1) = 9; entry (2,2) = 2(0) + 5(3) = 15.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v3::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v3::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"14","solution":"det M = (4)(5) - (3)(2) = 20 - 6 = 14.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v3::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1/14)[[5, -3], [-2, 4]]","solution":"Interchange the entries on the leading diagonal and change the sign of the other two, then divide by the determinant: M^-1 = (1/14)[[5, -3], [-2, 4]]. Check: M × M^-1 gives the identity matrix.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v3::d","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v3::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = 3, y = 1","solution":"The system is M(x, y) = (15, 11), so (x, y) = M^-1(15, 11) = (1/14)(5(15) + (-3)(11), (-2)(15) + 4(11)) = (1/14)(42, 14), giving x = 3 and y = 1. Check: 4(3) + 3(1) = 15.","criteria":null}}]'::jsonb,false,'draft')
on conflict(subject_id,rubric_version,paper_id) do nothing;
insert into spark_grading_private.rubrics_v2(subject_id,rubric_version,paper_id,criteria,active,verification_status)
values ('mathematics','source-scheme-draft-v2','original-v4','[{"id":"p2-q1-v4::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v4::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10","solution":"(2 1/6 + 3/4) = 13/6 + 3/4 = 26/12 + 9/12 = 35/12. (5/8 - 1/3) = 5/8 - 1/3 = 15/24 - 8/24 = 7/24. Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal, so 35/12 ÷ 7/24 = 35/12 × 24/7 = 10.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v4::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v4::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"960.00","solution":"Deposit = 20% of 4,800 = $960.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v4::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v4::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5220.00","solution":"Instalments = 12 × 355 = $4,260. Hire purchase price = 960.00 + 4,260 = $5220.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v4::b3","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v4::b3","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"8.75","solution":"Extra paid = 5220.00 - 4,800 = $420.00. As a percentage of the cash price this is (420.00 ÷ 4,800) × 100 = 8.75%.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v4::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v4::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(x - 7)/((x + 2)(x - 1))","solution":"The common denominator is (x + 2)(x - 1). The numerator is 3(x - 1) - 2(x + 2) = 3x - 3 - 2x - 4 = x - 7. So the single fraction is (x - 7)/((x + 2)(x - 1)).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v4::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"r = sqrt(3V/(πh))","solution":"Multiply both sides by 3: 3V = πr^2h. Divide by πh: r^2 = 3V/(πh). Take the positive square root: r = sqrt(3V/(πh)).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v4::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v4::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-37","solution":"3a^2 = 3(-3)^2 = 27 and b^3 = 4^3 = 64. The numerator is 27 - 64 = -37 and the denominator is -3 + 4 = 1. The value is -37.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v4::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v4::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"An enlargement, centre the origin (0, 0), with scale factor 3","solution":"Every image coordinate is 3 times the corresponding object coordinate: (1, 1) maps to (3, 3). The origin is the only point that does not move, so it is an enlargement of scale factor 3 about (0, 0).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v4::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3","solution":"Using the base and perpendicular height read from the grid, area = 1/2 × 2 × 3 = 3 square units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v4::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v4::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"27","solution":"Under an enlargement of scale factor k the area is multiplied by k^2. Area of B = 3^2 × 3 = 27 square units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v4::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v4::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-2","solution":"Gradient = (-5 - (7))/(4 - (-2)) = -12/6 = -2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v4::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1, 1)","solution":"Midpoint = ((-2 + 4)/2, (7 + -5)/2) = (1, 1).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v4::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v4::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"13.42","solution":"PQ = sqrt[(4 - (-2))^2 + (-5 - (7))^2] = sqrt(180) = 13.42 units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v4::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v4::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"y = -2x + 3","solution":"Using y - 7 = -2(x - (-2)) and simplifying gives y = -2x + 3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v4::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v4::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5, 18, 38, 52, 60","solution":"Add the frequencies in order: 5, 18, 38, 52, 60.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v4::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"A smooth curve through (10.5, 5), (20.5, 18), (30.5, 38), (40.5, 52), (50.5, 60)","solution":"Plot each cumulative frequency against the UPPER CLASS BOUNDARY of its class, 10.5, 20.5, 30.5, 40.5, 50.5, then join the points with a smooth curve.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v4::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v4::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"26.5","solution":"The median is the 30th value. Reading across from 30 on the vertical axis gives about 26.5 marks.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v4::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v4::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"17.3","solution":"Lower quartile: the 15th value, about 18.2. Upper quartile: the 45th value, about 35.5. Interquartile range = 35.5 - 18.2 = 17.3 marks.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v4::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v4::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"44","solution":"Arc = (120/360) x 2 x pi x r = (1/3) x 2 x (22/7) x 21 = (1/3) x 132 = 44 cm.","criteria":[]}},{"id":"p2-q6-v4::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"462","solution":"Area = (120/360) x pi x r^2 = (1/3) x (22/7) x 21^2 = (1/3) x 1386 = 462 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v4::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v4::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"86","solution":"The perimeter is the arc plus the two radii: 44 + 2(21) = 86 cm.","criteria":[]}},{"id":"p2-q6-v4::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v4::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"It is four times as large, because the area of a sector depends on the square of the radius","solution":"The area of a sector is a fixed fraction of pi r squared, so it varies as the square of the radius. Doubling the radius multiplies the area by 2 squared, that is by 4, giving 4 x 462 = 1848 cm squared.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","code":"B1","marks":1,"field":"answer","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"states that the area becomes four times as large","check":{"type":"prose","key":"four times as large","tokens":["four","4","times"],"mustHave":[],"forbid":["twice","double","doubles"],"polarity":"positive","quorum":0.5}},{"kind":"B","code":"B2","marks":1,"field":"answer","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"gives the square of the radius as the reason","check":{"type":"prose","key":"because the area depends on the square of the radius","tokens":["square","radius"],"mustHave":["square"],"forbid":[],"polarity":"positive","quorum":0.5}}]}},{"id":"p2-q7-v4::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v4::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4, 5, 9","solution":"Figure 4 has 4 dots in the top row and one more, 5, in the bottom row, giving 9 dots altogether.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v4::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"top n; bottom n + 1; total 2n + 1","solution":"The top row has n dots and the bottom row has n + 1. The total is n + (n + 1) = 2n + 1. Check with n = 3: 2(3) + 1 = 7, which matches the table.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v4::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v4::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"30","solution":"2n + 1 = 61, so 2n = 60 and n = 30.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v4::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v4::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"47","solution":"n + 1 = 24, so n = 23. The total is 2(23) + 1 = 47.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v4::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v4::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"0, -4, 5","solution":"When x = -1, y = 0; When x = 1, y = -4; When x = 4, y = 5.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v4::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"A smooth parabola through (-2, 5), (-1, 0), (0, -3), (1, -4), (2, -3), (3, 0), (4, 5)","solution":"Plot the points from the completed table and join them with a smooth curve, not a series of straight segments.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v4::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v4::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1, -4)","solution":"The curve is symmetrical about x = 1, the value halfway between the roots -1 and 3. There y = -4, so the minimum point is (1, -4).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v4::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v4::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = -1 and x = 3","solution":"The curve cuts the x-axis where y = 0, at x = -1 and x = 3. Check: (x + 1)(x - 3) = x^2 - 2x - 3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v4::e","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v4::e","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = -1.4 and x = 3.4","solution":"Draw the line y = 2 and read off where it meets the curve. The exact values are (2 ± sqrt(24))/2, that is -1.449 and 3.449, so -1.4 and 3.4 to 1 decimal place.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v4::a","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v4::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"12.9","solution":"By the cosine rule, KM^2 = 11^2 + 15^2 - 2(11)(15)cos 57° = 166.27, so KM = 12.89 = 12.9 cm.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v4::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"77","solution":"Use the cosine rule again, so that an obtuse angle is found correctly: cos(LKM) = (11^2 + 12.89^2 - 15^2) / (2 × 11 × 12.89), giving angle LKM = 77.3°, which is 77° to the nearest degree. Check: the three angles 57, 77.3 and 45.7 add to 180.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v4::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v4::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"69.2","solution":"Area = 1/2 × LK × LM × sin(KLM) = 1/2 × 11 × 15 × sin 57° = 69.19 = 69.2 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v4::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v4::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(-2, 3)","solution":"R(P) = (0(3) + (-1)(2), 1(3) + 0(2)) = (-2, 3). Check: the distance from the origin is unchanged.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v4::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"2.5","solution":"T(4, -3) = (4k, -3k) = (10, -7.5), so 4k = 10 and k = 2.5. Check: -3 × 2.5 = -7.5.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v4::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v4::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"[[0, -2.5], [2.5, 0]]","solution":"Doing R first and then T is represented by the product TR (the second transformation on the left): TR = [[2.5, 0], [0, 2.5]] × [[0, -1], [1, 0]] = [[0, -2.5], [2.5, 0]].","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v4::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v4::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"6.25; areas are multiplied by 6.25","solution":"det = (0)(0) - (-2.5)(2.5) = 6.25. The determinant of a transformation matrix is the factor by which areas are multiplied, so every area is multiplied by 6.25. The rotation alone does not change area, and the enlargement multiplies it by k^2.","criteria":null}}]'::jsonb,false,'draft')
on conflict(subject_id,rubric_version,paper_id) do nothing;
insert into spark_grading_private.rubrics_v2(subject_id,rubric_version,paper_id,criteria,active,verification_status)
values ('mathematics','source-scheme-draft-v2','original-v5','[{"id":"p2-q1-v5::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"32/5","solution":"(4 1/2 - 1 5/6) = 9/2 - 11/6 = 27/6 - 11/6 = 8/3. (3/4 - 1/3) = 3/4 - 1/3 = 9/12 - 4/12 = 5/12. Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal, so 8/3 ÷ 5/12 = 8/3 × 12/5 = 32/5. As a mixed number this is 6 2/5.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v5::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v5::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"252.00","solution":"Overtime hours = 47 - 40 = 7. Overtime rate = 1.5 × 24 = $36.00 per hour. Overtime pay = 7 × 36.00 = $252.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v5::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v5::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"1212.00","solution":"Basic pay = 40 × 24 = $960. Total wage = 960 + 252.00 = $1212.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v5::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5520.00","solution":"Taxable income = 46,000 - 18,400 = $27,600. Tax = 20% of 27,600 = $5520.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v5::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(x - 15)/((x + 1)(x - 3))","solution":"The common denominator is (x + 1)(x - 3). The numerator is 4(x - 3) - 3(x + 1) = 4x - 12 - 3x - 3 = x - 15. So the single fraction is (x - 15)/((x + 1)(x - 3)).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v5::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"r = sqrt(3V/(πh))","solution":"Multiply both sides by 3: 3V = πr^2h. Divide by πh: r^2 = 3V/(πh). Take the positive square root: r = sqrt(3V/(πh)).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v5::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-25","solution":"3a^2 = 3(-6)^2 = 108 and b^3 = 2^3 = 8. The numerator is 108 - 8 = 100 and the denominator is -6 + 2 = -4. The value is -25.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v5::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"An enlargement, centre the origin (0, 0), with scale factor 2","solution":"Every image coordinate is 2 times the corresponding object coordinate: (1, 2) maps to (2, 4). The origin is the only point that does not move, so it is an enlargement of scale factor 2 about (0, 0).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v5::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3","solution":"Using the base and perpendicular height read from the grid, area = 1/2 × 3 × 2 = 3 square units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v5::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"12","solution":"Under an enlargement of scale factor k the area is multiplied by k^2. Area of B = 2^2 × 3 = 12 square units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v5::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3/4","solution":"Gradient = (7 - (1))/(5 - (-3)) = 6/8 = 3/4.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v5::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1, 4)","solution":"Midpoint = ((-3 + 5)/2, (1 + 7)/2) = (1, 4).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v5::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10.00","solution":"PQ = sqrt[(5 - (-3))^2 + (7 - (1))^2] = sqrt(100) = 10.00 units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v5::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v5::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"y = 3x/4 + 13/4","solution":"Using y - 1 = 3/4(x - (-3)) and simplifying gives y = 3x/4 + 13/4.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v5::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4, 14, 30, 52, 70, 80","solution":"Add the frequencies in order: 4, 14, 30, 52, 70, 80.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v5::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"A smooth curve through (10.5, 4), (20.5, 14), (30.5, 30), (40.5, 52), (50.5, 70), (60.5, 80)","solution":"Plot each cumulative frequency against the UPPER CLASS BOUNDARY of its class, 10.5, 20.5, 30.5, 40.5, 50.5, 60.5, then join the points with a smooth curve.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v5::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"35.0","solution":"The median is the 40th value. Reading across from 40 on the vertical axis gives about 35.0 marks.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v5::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v5::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"20.7","solution":"Find the 20th and 60th values on the cumulative-frequency curve. Using linear interpolation between the plotted class-boundary points gives Q1 = 20.5 + (20 - 14)/(30 - 14) × 10 = 24.25 and Q3 = 40.5 + (60 - 52)/(70 - 52) × 10 ≈ 44.944. Calculate the range before rounding: 44.944 - 24.25 ≈ 20.694, so the estimated interquartile range is 20.7 marks. A graph reading can vary slightly with the drawing.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v5::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"22","solution":"Arc = (90/360) x 2 x pi x r = (1/4) x 2 x (22/7) x 14 = (1/4) x 88 = 22 cm.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v5::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"154","solution":"Area = (90/360) x pi x r^2 = (1/4) x (22/7) x 14^2 = (1/4) x 616 = 154 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v5::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"50","solution":"The perimeter is the arc plus the two radii: 22 + 2(14) = 50 cm.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v5::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4, 5, 9","solution":"Figure 4 has 4 dots in the top row and one more, 5, in the bottom row, giving 9 dots altogether.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v5::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"top n; bottom n + 1; total 2n + 1","solution":"The top row has n dots and the bottom row has n + 1. The total is n + (n + 1) = 2n + 1. Check with n = 3: 2(3) + 1 = 7, which matches the table.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v5::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"43","solution":"2n + 1 = 87, so 2n = 86 and n = 43.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v5::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v5::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"61","solution":"n + 1 = 31, so n = 30. The total is 2(30) + 1 = 61.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v5::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"0, -8, 7","solution":"When x = -2, y = 0; When x = 0, y = -8; When x = 5, y = 7.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v5::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"A smooth parabola through (-3, 7), (-2, 0), (-1, -5), (0, -8), (1, -9), (2, -8), (3, -5), (4, 0), (5, 7)","solution":"Plot the points from the completed table and join them with a smooth curve, not a series of straight segments.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v5::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1, -9)","solution":"The curve is symmetrical about x = 1, the value halfway between the roots -2 and 4. There y = -9, so the minimum point is (1, -9).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v5::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v5::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = -2 and x = 4","solution":"The curve cuts the x-axis where y = 0, at x = -2 and x = 4. Check: (x + 2)(x - 4) = x^2 - 2x - 8.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v5::e","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v5::e","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = -2.5 and x = 4.5","solution":"Draw the line y = 3 and read off where it meets the curve. The exact values are (2 ± sqrt(48))/2, that is -2.464 and 4.464, so -2.5 and 4.5 to 1 decimal place.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v5::a","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"17.6","solution":"By the cosine rule, KM^2 = 8^2 + 13^2 - 2(8)(13)cos 112° = 310.92, so KM = 17.63 = 17.6 cm.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v5::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"43","solution":"Use the cosine rule again, so that an obtuse angle is found correctly: cos(LKM) = (8^2 + 17.63^2 - 13^2) / (2 × 8 × 17.63), giving angle LKM = 43.1°, which is 43° to the nearest degree. Check: the three angles 112, 43.1 and 24.9 add to 180.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v5::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"48.2","solution":"Area = 1/2 × LK × LM × sin(KLM) = 1/2 × 8 × 13 × sin 112° = 48.21 = 48.2 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v5::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(-5, 2)","solution":"R(P) = (0(2) + (-1)(5), 1(2) + 0(5)) = (-5, 2). Check: the distance from the origin is unchanged.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v5::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3","solution":"T(-2, 4) = (-2k, 4k) = (-6, 12), so -2k = -6 and k = 3. Check: 4 × 3 = 12.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v5::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"[[0, -3], [3, 0]]","solution":"Doing R first and then T is represented by the product TR (the second transformation on the left): TR = [[3, 0], [0, 3]] × [[0, -1], [1, 0]] = [[0, -3], [3, 0]].","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v5::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v5::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"9; areas are multiplied by 9","solution":"det = (0)(0) - (-3)(3) = 9. The determinant of a transformation matrix is the factor by which areas are multiplied, so every area is multiplied by 9. The rotation alone does not change area, and the enlargement multiplies it by k^2.","criteria":null}}]'::jsonb,false,'draft')
