values ('mathematics','source-scheme-draft-v2','original-v6','[{"id":"p2-q1-v6::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"41/5","solution":"(2 3/5 + 1 1/2) = 13/5 + 3/2 = 26/10 + 15/10 = 41/10. (4/5 - 3/10) = 4/5 - 3/10 = 8/10 - 3/10 = 1/2. Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal, so 41/10 ÷ 1/2 = 41/10 × 2 = 41/5. As a mixed number this is 8 1/5.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v6::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v6::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"576.00","solution":"Overtime hours = 44 - 35 = 9. Overtime rate = 2 × 32 = $64.00 per hour. Overtime pay = 9 × 64.00 = $576.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v6::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v6::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"1696.00","solution":"Basic pay = 35 × 32 = $1,120. Total wage = 1,120 + 576.00 = $1696.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v6::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"9125.00","solution":"Taxable income = 58,000 - 21,500 = $36,500. Tax = 25% of 36,500 = $9125.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v6::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(3x - 16)/((x + 3)(x - 2))","solution":"The common denominator is (x + 3)(x - 2). The numerator is 5(x - 2) - 2(x + 3) = 5x - 10 - 2x - 6 = 3x - 16. So the single fraction is (3x - 16)/((x + 3)(x - 2)).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v6::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"r = sqrt(3V/(πh))","solution":"Multiply both sides by 3: 3V = πr^2h. Divide by πh: r^2 = 3V/(πh). Take the positive square root: r = sqrt(3V/(πh)).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v6::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-21","solution":"3a^2 = 3(-4)^2 = 48 and b^3 = 3^3 = 27. The numerator is 48 - 27 = 21 and the denominator is -4 + 3 = -1. The value is -21.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v6::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"An enlargement, centre the origin (0, 0), with scale factor 2","solution":"Every image coordinate is 2 times the corresponding object coordinate: (2, 1) maps to (4, 2). The origin is the only point that does not move, so it is an enlargement of scale factor 2 about (0, 0).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v6::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3","solution":"Using the base and perpendicular height read from the grid, area = 1/2 × 2 × 3 = 3 square units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v6::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"12","solution":"Under an enlargement of scale factor k the area is multiplied by k^2. Area of B = 2^2 × 3 = 12 square units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v6::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"2","solution":"Gradient = (8 - (-4))/(7 - (1)) = 12/6 = 2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v6::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(4, 2)","solution":"Midpoint = ((1 + 7)/2, (-4 + 8)/2) = (4, 2).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v6::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"13.42","solution":"PQ = sqrt[(7 - (1))^2 + (8 - (-4))^2] = sqrt(180) = 13.42 units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v6::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v6::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"y = 2x - 6","solution":"Using y - -4 = 2(x - (1)) and simplifying gives y = 2x - 6.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v6::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"45","solution":"Angles at the centre of a circle add up to 360°, so the remaining angle is 360 - (105 + 135 + 75) = 45°.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v6::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"70","solution":"The Bus sector is 105/360 of the circle, so the number of people is (105/360) × 240 = 70.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v6::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"Car","solution":"Car has the largest sector angle, 135°, and the number of people is proportional to the angle.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v6::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v6::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"1/8","solution":"30 of the 240 people chose Walk, so the probability is 30/240 = 1/8.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v6::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"44","solution":"Arc = (60/360) x 2 x pi x r = (1/6) x 2 x (22/7) x 42 = (1/6) x 264 = 44 cm.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v6::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"924","solution":"Area = (60/360) x pi x r^2 = (1/6) x (22/7) x 42^2 = (1/6) x 5544 = 924 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v6::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"128","solution":"The perimeter is the arc plus the two radii: 44 + 2(42) = 128 cm.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v6::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5 × 7 + 6 = 41","solution":"The first number is the statement number, the second is 2 more and the number added is 1 more. So the 5th statement is 5 × 7 + 6 = 41.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v6::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10 × 12 + 11 = 131","solution":"10 × 12 + 11 = 120 + 11 = 131.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v6::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"n × (n + 2) + (n + 1) = n^2 + 3n + 1","solution":"The nth statement is n × (n + 2) + (n + 1). Expanding, n(n + 2) = n^2 + 2n, so the value is n^2 + 2n + n + 1 = n^2 + 3n + 1. Check with n = 4: 16 + 12 + 1 = 29, which matches the table.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v6::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v6::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"7","solution":"n^2 + 3n + 1 = 71, so n^2 + 3n - 70 = 0, which factorises to (n + 10)(n - 7) = 0. Since n must be positive, n = 7. Check: 7 × 9 + 8 = 71.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v6::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"2x + 3y ≤ 60; x ≥ 6; y ≥ 4","solution":"Cloth: 2x + 3y ≤ 60. At least 6 shirts: x ≥ 6. At least 4 pairs of trousers: y ≥ 4.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v6::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(6, 4); (6, 16); (24, 4)","solution":"The region is bounded by x = 6, y = 4 and 2x + 3y = 60. Taking the lines in pairs gives (6, 4), (6, 16), (24, 4).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v6::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"P = 50x + 60y","solution":"P = 50x + 60y.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v6::d","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v6::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"$1440, from 24 shirts and 4 pairs of trousers","solution":"The maximum of a linear expression over a polygon occurs at a vertex. Testing each: P(6, 4) = 540; P(6, 16) = 1260; P(24, 4) = 1440. The maximum profit is $1440, making 24 shirts and 4 pairs of trousers.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v6::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"47 degrees, by the alternate segment theorem: the angle between the tangent and the chord TA equals the angle that chord subtends in the alternate segment","solution":"By the alternate segment theorem, the angle between a tangent and a chord equals the angle that the chord subtends in the alternate segment. Angle ABT stands on the chord TA in that segment, so x = 47.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v6::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"72","solution":"In triangle ABT the three angles are 47°, 61° and angle ATB, so angle ATB = 180 - 47 - 61 = 72°.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v6::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"61 degrees, by the alternate segment theorem: the chord TB subtends this angle in the alternate segment","solution":"The chord TB subtends angle TAB = 61° in the alternate segment, so the angle between the tangent and TB is also 61°. Check: 47 + 72 + 61 = 180, the angles on the straight line at T.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v6::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v6::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"A tangent is perpendicular to the radius at the point of contact","solution":"A tangent to a circle meets the radius drawn to the point of contact at a right angle. OT is that radius, so angle between OT and the tangent is 90°.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v6::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"b - a","solution":"\\vec{AB} = \\vec{AO} + \\vec{OB} = -a + b = b - a.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v6::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1/2)(b - a)","solution":"\\vec{OM} = (1/2)a and \\vec{ON} = (1/2)b, so \\vec{MN} = \\vec{ON} - \\vec{OM} = (1/2)b - (1/2)a = (1/2)(b - a).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v6::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"MN is parallel to AB and MN is half the length of AB","solution":"\\vec{MN} = (1/2)\\vec{AB}, so MN is a scalar multiple of AB. Two vectors that are scalar multiples of one another are parallel, so MN is parallel to AB, and since the scalar is 1/2, MN is half as long as AB.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v6::d","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v6::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"\\vec{AP} = b = \\vec{OB}, so OAPB is a parallelogram","solution":"\\vec{AP} = \\vec{OP} - \\vec{OA} = (a + b) - a = b, and \\vec{OB} = b. So AP and OB are equal in length and parallel. A quadrilateral with one pair of opposite sides equal and parallel is a parallelogram, so OAPB is a parallelogram.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","code":"B1","marks":2,"field":"all","depends":[],"profile":"algorithmic","description":"finds AP in terms of a and b","check":{"type":"written","any":["ap","vector ap"],"all":[["b"]]}},{"kind":"B","code":"B2","marks":1,"field":"all","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"states that AP and OB are equal and parallel","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"written","any":["equal","same","equals","parallel"]},{"type":"method","any":["= b =","=b=","ap = ob","ap=ob"]}]}},{"kind":"B","code":"B3","marks":1,"field":"all","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"concludes that OAPB is a parallelogram","check":{"type":"written","any":["parallelogram"],"none":["trapezium","rhombus","not a parallelogram"]}}]}}]'::jsonb,false,'draft')
on conflict(subject_id,rubric_version,paper_id) do nothing;
insert into spark_grading_private.rubrics_v2(subject_id,rubric_version,paper_id,criteria,active,verification_status)
values ('mathematics','source-scheme-draft-v2','original-v7','[{"id":"p2-q1-v7::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"7/2","solution":"(5 1/4 - 2 5/8) = 21/4 - 21/8 = 42/8 - 21/8. (7/12 + 1/6) = 7/12 + 1/6 = 7/12 + 2/12 = 3/4. Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal, so 21/8 ÷ 3/4 = 21/8 × 4/3 = 7/2. As a mixed number this is 3 1/2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v7::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v7::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"38016.00","solution":"Value = 240 × 158.40 = J$38016.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v7::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v7::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"38776.32","solution":"Commission = 2% of 38016.00 = J$760.32. Total = 38016.00 + 760.32 = J$38776.32.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v7::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"450.00","solution":"500 mL = 0.5 litre. Cost per litre = 225 ÷ 0.5 = $450.00. For comparison the large bottle costs 720 ÷ 1.8 = $400.00 per litre, so the large bottle is the better buy.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v7::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-x^2 + 13x - 6","solution":"(3x - 2)(x + 5) = 3x^2 + 15x - 2x - 10 = 3x^2 + 13x - 10. Also -4(x^2 - 1) = -4x^2 + 4. Adding gives -x^2 + 13x - 6.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v7::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(2b - 3)(2a + 5)","solution":"Group the first two terms and the last two: (4ab - 6a) + (10b - 15). Take 2a out of the first bracket and 5 out of the second: 2a(2b - 3) + 5(2b - 3). Both terms now share the factor (2b - 3), so 4ab - 6a + 10b - 15 = (2b - 3)(2a + 5).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v7::c1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v7::c1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x < 7","solution":"3x - 6 < x + 8, so 2x < 14 and x < 7.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v7::c2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v7::c2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"6","solution":"x must be strictly less than 7, so the greatest integer is 6.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v7::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(x, y) maps to (y, -x)","solution":"A quarter turn clockwise about O interchanges the coordinates and changes one sign: (x, y) maps to (y, -x).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v7::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1, -2); (1, -6); (4, -2)","solution":"Applying the rule to each vertex: (2, 1) -> (1, -2); (6, 1) -> (1, -6); (2, 4) -> (4, -2).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v7::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1, -4)","solution":"The midpoint is ((2 + 6)/2, (1 + 1)/2) = (4, 1). Applying the rule gives (1, -4). A rotation maps the midpoint of a side onto the midpoint of the image of that side.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v7::a","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3","solution":"Parallel lines have equal gradients, so the gradient is 3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v7::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-1/3","solution":"Perpendicular gradients multiply to -1, so the gradient is -1/(3) = -1/3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v7::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"y = 3x - 17","solution":"Using y - (1) = 3(x - 6) gives y = 3x - 17.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v7::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v7::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"y = -x/3 + 3","solution":"Using y - (1) = -1/3(x - 6) gives y = -x/3 + 3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v7::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"48","solution":"Angles at the centre of a circle add up to 360°, so the remaining angle is 360 - (150 + 90 + 72) = 48°.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v7::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"45","solution":"The Cricket sector is 90/360 of the circle, so the number of people is (90/360) × 180 = 45.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v7::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"Football","solution":"Football has the largest sector angle, 150°, and the number of people is proportional to the angle.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v7::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v7::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"2/15","solution":"24 of the 180 people chose Netball, so the probability is 24/180 = 2/15.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v7::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"24","solution":"Area = 1/2 × 8 × 6 = 24 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v7::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"480","solution":"Volume = area of cross-section × length = 24 × 20 = 480 cm^3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v7::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10","solution":"By Pythagoras'' theorem the hypotenuse is sqrt(8^2 + 6^2) = sqrt(100) = 10 cm.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v7::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v7::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"528","solution":"Two triangular ends: 2 × 24 = 48 cm^2. The perimeter of the cross-section is 8 + 6 + 10 = 24 cm, so the three rectangles give 24 × 20 = 480 cm^2. Total = 528 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v7::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5 × 7 + 6 = 41","solution":"The first number is the statement number, the second is 2 more and the number added is 1 more. So the 5th statement is 5 × 7 + 6 = 41.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v7::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10 × 12 + 11 = 131","solution":"10 × 12 + 11 = 120 + 11 = 131.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v7::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"n × (n + 2) + (n + 1) = n^2 + 3n + 1","solution":"The nth statement is n × (n + 2) + (n + 1). Expanding, n(n + 2) = n^2 + 2n, so the value is n^2 + 2n + n + 1 = n^2 + 3n + 1. Check with n = 4: 16 + 12 + 1 = 29, which matches the table.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v7::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v7::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10","solution":"n^2 + 3n + 1 = 131, so n^2 + 3n - 130 = 0, which factorises to (n + 13)(n - 10) = 0. Since n must be positive, n = 10. Check: 10 × 12 + 11 = 131.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v7::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3x + 2y ≤ 72; x ≥ 6; y ≥ 6","solution":"Timber: 3x + 2y ≤ 72. At least 6 tables: x ≥ 6. At least 6 chairs: y ≥ 6.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v7::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(6, 6); (6, 27); (20, 6)","solution":"The region is bounded by x = 6, y = 6 and 3x + 2y = 72. Taking the lines in pairs gives (6, 6), (6, 27), (20, 6).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v7::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"P = 40x + 30y","solution":"P = 40x + 30y.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v7::d","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v7::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"$1050, from 6 tables and 27 chairs","solution":"The maximum of a linear expression over a polygon occurs at a vertex. Testing each: P(6, 6) = 420; P(6, 27) = 1050; P(20, 6) = 980. The maximum profit is $1050, making 6 tables and 27 chairs.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v7::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"52 degrees, by the alternate segment theorem: the angle between the tangent and the chord TA equals the angle that chord subtends in the alternate segment","solution":"By the alternate segment theorem, the angle between a tangent and a chord equals the angle that the chord subtends in the alternate segment. Angle ABT stands on the chord TA in that segment, so x = 52.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v7::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"70","solution":"In triangle ABT the three angles are 52°, 58° and angle ATB, so angle ATB = 180 - 52 - 58 = 70°.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v7::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"58 degrees, by the alternate segment theorem: the chord TB subtends this angle in the alternate segment","solution":"The chord TB subtends angle TAB = 58° in the alternate segment, so the angle between the tangent and TB is also 58°. Check: 52 + 70 + 58 = 180, the angles on the straight line at T.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v7::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v7::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"A tangent is perpendicular to the radius at the point of contact","solution":"A tangent to a circle meets the radius drawn to the point of contact at a right angle. OT is that radius, so angle between OT and the tangent is 90°.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v7::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"b - a","solution":"\\vec{AB} = \\vec{AO} + \\vec{OB} = -a + b = b - a.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v7::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1/2)(b - a)","solution":"\\vec{OM} = (1/2)a and \\vec{ON} = (1/2)b, so \\vec{MN} = \\vec{ON} - \\vec{OM} = (1/2)b - (1/2)a = (1/2)(b - a).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v7::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"MN is parallel to AB and MN is half the length of AB","solution":"\\vec{MN} = (1/2)\\vec{AB}, so MN is a scalar multiple of AB. Two vectors that are scalar multiples of one another are parallel, so MN is parallel to AB, and since the scalar is 1/2, MN is half as long as AB.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v7::d","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v7::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"\\vec{AP} = b = \\vec{OB}, so OAPB is a parallelogram","solution":"\\vec{AP} = \\vec{OP} - \\vec{OA} = (a + b) - a = b, and \\vec{OB} = b. So AP and OB are equal in length and parallel. A quadrilateral with one pair of opposite sides equal and parallel is a parallelogram, so OAPB is a parallelogram.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","code":"B1","marks":2,"field":"all","depends":[],"profile":"algorithmic","description":"finds AP in terms of a and b","check":{"type":"written","any":["ap","vector ap"],"all":[["b"]]}},{"kind":"B","code":"B2","marks":1,"field":"all","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"states that AP and OB are equal and parallel","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"written","any":["equal","same","equals","parallel"]},{"type":"method","any":["= b =","=b=","ap = ob","ap=ob"]}]}},{"kind":"B","code":"B3","marks":1,"field":"all","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"concludes that OAPB is a parallelogram","check":{"type":"written","any":["parallelogram"],"none":["trapezium","rhombus","not a parallelogram"]}}]}}]'::jsonb,false,'draft')
on conflict(subject_id,rubric_version,paper_id) do nothing;
insert into spark_grading_private.rubrics_v2(subject_id,rubric_version,paper_id,criteria,active,verification_status)
values ('mathematics','source-scheme-draft-v2','original-v8','[{"id":"p2-q1-v8::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"7/2","solution":"(1 5/6 + 2 1/4) = 11/6 + 9/4 = 22/12 + 27/12 = 49/12. (5/6 + 1/3) = 5/6 + 1/3 = 5/6 + 2/6 = 7/6. Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal, so 49/12 ÷ 7/6 = 49/12 × 6/7 = 7/2. As a mixed number this is 3 1/2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v8::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v8::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"28350.00","solution":"Value = 180 × 157.50 = J$28350.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v8::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v8::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"29200.50","solution":"Commission = 3% of 28350.00 = J$850.50. Total = 28350.00 + 850.50 = J$29200.50.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v8::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v8::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"420.00","solution":"400 mL = 0.4 litre. Cost per litre = 168 ÷ 0.4 = $420.00. For comparison the large bottle costs 950 ÷ 2.5 = $380.00 per litre, so the large bottle is the better buy.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v8::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-x^2 + 5x - 9","solution":"(2x - 3)(x + 4) = 2x^2 + 8x - 3x - 12 = 2x^2 + 5x - 12. Also -3(x^2 - 1) = -3x^2 + 3. Adding gives -x^2 + 5x - 9.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v8::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v8::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(2b - 3)(3a + 2)","solution":"Group the first two terms and the last two: (6ab - 9a) + (4b - 6). Take 3a out of the first bracket and 2 out of the second: 3a(2b - 3) + 2(2b - 3). Both terms now share the factor (2b - 3), so 6ab - 9a + 4b - 6 = (2b - 3)(3a + 2).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v8::c1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v8::c1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x < 7","solution":"4x - 12 < x + 9, so 3x < 21 and x < 7.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v8::c2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v8::c2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"6","solution":"x must be strictly less than 7, so the greatest integer is 6.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v8::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(x, y) maps to (-y, x)","solution":"A quarter turn anticlockwise about O interchanges the coordinates and changes one sign: (x, y) maps to (-y, x).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v8::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v8::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(-2, 1); (-2, 5); (-6, 1)","solution":"Applying the rule to each vertex: (1, 2) -> (-2, 1); (5, 2) -> (-2, 5); (1, 6) -> (-6, 1).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v8::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v8::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(-2, 3)","solution":"The midpoint is ((1 + 5)/2, (2 + 2)/2) = (3, 2). Applying the rule gives (-2, 3). A rotation maps the midpoint of a side onto the midpoint of the image of that side.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v8::a","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-2","solution":"Parallel lines have equal gradients, so the gradient is -2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v8::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v8::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"1/2","solution":"Perpendicular gradients multiply to -1, so the gradient is -1/(-2) = 1/2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v8::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v8::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"y = -2x + 9","solution":"Using y - (1) = -2(x - 4) gives y = -2x + 9.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v8::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v8::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"y = x/2 - 1","solution":"Using y - (1) = 1/2(x - 4) gives y = x/2 - 1.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v8::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5/12","solution":"There are 12 marbles altogether and 5 of them are red, so the probability is 5/12.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v8::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v8::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"2/3","solution":"5 + 3 = 8 marbles are not green, so the probability is 8/12 = 2/3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v8::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v8::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5/33","solution":"P(first red) = 5/12. After a red marble is removed there are 4 red marbles out of 11, so P(second red) = 4/11. Multiplying, P(both red) = (5/12) × (4/11) = 5/33.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v8::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v8::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5/44","solution":"P = (5/12) × (3/11) = 5/44.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v8::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"30","solution":"Area = 1/2 × 12 × 5 = 30 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v8::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v8::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"750","solution":"Volume = area of cross-section × length = 30 × 25 = 750 cm^3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v8::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v8::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"13","solution":"By Pythagoras'' theorem the hypotenuse is sqrt(12^2 + 5^2) = sqrt(169) = 13 cm.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v8::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v8::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"810","solution":"Two triangular ends: 2 × 30 = 60 cm^2. The perimeter of the cross-section is 12 + 5 + 13 = 30 cm, so the three rectangles give 30 × 25 = 750 cm^2. Total = 810 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v8::a","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4","solution":"Each term is 4 more than the one before.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v8::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v8::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4n + 3","solution":"T_n = a + (n - 1)d = 7 + (n - 1)(4) = 4n + 3. Check with n = 1: 4(1) + 3 = 7.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v8::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v8::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"51","solution":"T_12 = 7 + (12 - 1)(4) = 51.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v8::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v8::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"900","solution":"S_n = (n/2)[2a + (n - 1)d], so S_20 = (20/2)[2(7) + (20 - 1)(4)] = 900.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v8::e","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v8::e","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"the 19th term","solution":"Set 4n + 3 = 79. Then 4n = 76 and n = 19, so 79 is the 19th term.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v8::a","maxMarks":5,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = 3.89 and x = -0.39","solution":"Using x = [-b ± sqrt(b^2 - 4ac)]/(2a) with a = 2, b = -7 and c = -3: b^2 - 4ac = 49 - 4(2)(-3) = 73, and sqrt(73) = 8.5440. So x = (7 ± 8.5440)/4, giving x = 3.89 or x = -0.39.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v8::b1","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v8::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x^2 - x - 6 = 0","solution":"At a point of intersection the two y-values are equal, so x^2 + 2x - 5 = 3x + 1. Collecting all the terms on one side gives x^2 - x - 6 = 0.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","code":"M1","marks":1,"field":"working","depends":[],"profile":"algorithmic","description":"equates the line and the curve","check":{"type":"containsEquivalentExpression","value":"x^2 + 2x - 5"}},{"kind":"M","code":"M2","marks":1,"field":"working","depends":["M1"],"profile":"algorithmic","description":"collects every term on one side","check":{"type":"containsEquivalentExpression","value":"(x^2 + 2x - 5) - (3x + 1)"}},{"kind":"A","code":"A1","marks":1,"field":"answer","depends":["M2"],"strictDepends":true,"profile":"algorithmic","description":"reaches x^2 - x - 6 = 0","check":{"type":"equation","value":"x^2 - x - 6 = 0"}}]}},{"id":"p2-q8-v8::b2","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v8::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(-2, -5) and (3, 10)","solution":"Factorising, (x + 2)(x - 3) = 0, so x = -2 or x = 3. Substituting into y = 3x + 1 gives y = -5 and y = 10. The points are (-2, -5) and (3, 10).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v8::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"52.0","solution":"A bearing is measured clockwise from north, so the northerly component is 60 cos 210° = -51.96. Q is 52.0 km south of P.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v8::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v8::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"30.0","solution":"The easterly component is 60 sin 210° = -30.00, so Q is 30.0 km west of P. Check: 52.0^2 + 30.0^2 gives 60^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v8::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v8::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"100.0","solution":"Adding the components of the second leg, R is -91.96 km north and 39.28 km east of P. So PR = sqrt(-91.96^2 + 39.28^2) = 100.0 km.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v8::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v8::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"157","solution":"tan(bearing) = east / north = 39.28 / -91.96, so the bearing of R from P is 156.9°, that is 157° to the nearest degree.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v8::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(4, 8)","solution":"\\vec{AB} = \\vec{OB} - \\vec{OA} = (7 - 3, 9 - 1) = (4, 8).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v8::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v8::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"8.94","solution":"|\\vec{AB}| = sqrt(4^2 + 8^2) = sqrt(80) = 8.94 units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v8::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v8::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(4, 3)","solution":"AC : CB = 1 : 3, so \\vec{AC} = (1/4)\\vec{AB} = (1, 2). Then \\vec{OC} = \\vec{OA} + \\vec{AC} = (4, 3).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v8::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v8::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"not parallel","solution":"\\vec{OC} = (4, 3) and \\vec{AB} = (4, 8). For them to be parallel we would need 4 × 8 = 3 × 4, that is 32 = 12, which is false. So they are not parallel.","criteria":null}}]'::jsonb,false,'draft')
