values ('mathematics','source-scheme-draft-v2','original-v9','[{"id":"p2-q1-v9::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"54/5","solution":"(3 3/4 - 1 1/2) = 15/4 - 3/2 = 15/4 - 6/4 = 9/4. (3/8 - 1/6) = 3/8 - 1/6 = 9/24 - 4/24 = 5/24. Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal, so 9/4 ÷ 5/24 = 9/4 × 24/5 = 54/5. As a mixed number this is 10 4/5.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v9::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v9::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3000.00","solution":"Total parts = 2 + 3 + 5 = 10. One part = 6,000 / 10 = $600.00. Largest share = 5 x 600.00 = $3000.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v9::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v9::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"1800.00","solution":"Smallest share = 2 x 600.00 = $1200.00. Difference = 3000.00 - 1200.00 = $1800.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v9::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10","solution":"The job needs 8 × 15 = 120 worker-days. With 12 workers this takes 120 ÷ 12 = 10 days.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v9::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3x + 2y = 32; 5x + 4y = 58","solution":"From the first purchase, 3x + 2y = 32. From the second, 5x + 4y = 58.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v9::b","maxMarks":5,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v9::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"notebook $6.00, pen $7.00","solution":"Multiply the first equation by 5 and the second by 3 to eliminate x, or use substitution. Solving gives x = 6 and y = 7. Check: 3(6) + 2(7) = 32 and 5(6) + 4(7) = 58.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v9::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"71","solution":"Total = 6(6) + 5(7) = $71.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v9::a","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"A correct construction of triangle PQR","solution":"Draw PQ = 8 cm. At Q construct an angle of 60° using compass arcs only (an equilateral-triangle arc gives 60°). Mark R on that arm with QR = 6 cm and join PR.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v9::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v9::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"7.2","solution":"By the cosine rule the true length is PR^2 = 8^2 + 6^2 - 2(8)(6)cos 60° = 52.00, so PR = 7.21 cm. A measurement of 7.2 cm is expected.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v9::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"20.8","solution":"Area = 1/2 × PQ × QR × sin(angle PQR) = 1/2 × 8 × 6 × sin 60° = 20.8 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v9::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-5, -3, -1, 1, 3","solution":"Substituting each value of x in turn: f(-2) = -5; f(-1) = -3; f(0) = -1; f(1) = 1; f(2) = 3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v9::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v9::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"{-5, -3, -1, 1, 3}","solution":"The range is the set of output values: {-5, -3, -1, 1, 3}.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v9::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = 5; not in the domain","solution":"2x - 1 = 9 gives 2x = 10 and x = 5. This value is not in the given domain.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v9::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v9::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"Yes, one-to-one, because every member of the domain gives a different value of f(x), so no two members map onto the same member of the range","solution":"Every value of x gives a different value of f(x), because the relation is linear with a non-zero gradient, so no two members of the domain map onto the same member of the range. The relation is therefore one-to-one.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","code":"B1","marks":1,"field":"answer","depends":[],"profile":"conceptual","description":"states that the relation is one-to-one","check":{"type":"written","any":["one to one","one-to-one","1-1","yes"],"none":["many to one","many-to-one","not one to one"]}},{"kind":"B","code":"B2","marks":1,"field":"all","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"gives a valid reason","check":{"type":"written","any":["different","distinct","no two","each x","every x","unique","linear","non-zero gradient","not repeated","no repeated","each member of the domain","one output"]}}]}},{"id":"p2-q5-v9::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4/15","solution":"There are 15 marbles altogether and 4 of them are red, so the probability is 4/15.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v9::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v9::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"2/3","solution":"4 + 6 = 10 marbles are not green, so the probability is 10/15 = 2/3.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v9::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"2/35","solution":"P(first red) = 4/15. After a red marble is removed there are 3 red marbles out of 14, so P(second red) = 3/14. Multiplying, P(both red) = (4/15) × (3/14) = 2/35.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v9::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v9::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4/35","solution":"P = (4/15) × (6/14) = 4/35.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v9::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"32.4","solution":"tan 34° = TB / 48, so TB = 48 tan 34° = 32.38 = 32.4 m.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v9::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v9::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"57.9","solution":"cos 34° = 48 / AT, so AT = 48 / cos 34° = 57.90 = 57.9 m.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v9::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"25","solution":"tan(angle) = TB / 68 = 32.38 / 68 = 0.4761, so the angle of elevation is 25.5°, which is 25° to the nearest degree. It is smaller than 34°, as expected, because C is further from the tower.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v9::a","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5","solution":"Each term is 5 more than the one before.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v9::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v9::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5n + 8","solution":"T_n = a + (n - 1)d = 13 + (n - 1)(5) = 5n + 8. Check with n = 1: 5(1) + 8 = 13.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v9::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"88","solution":"T_16 = 13 + (16 - 1)(5) = 88.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v9::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v9::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"999","solution":"S_n = (n/2)[2a + (n - 1)d], so S_18 = (18/2)[2(13) + (18 - 1)(5)] = 999.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v9::e","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v9::e","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"the 18th term","solution":"Set 5n + 8 = 98. Then 5n = 90 and n = 18, so 98 is the 18th term.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v9::a","maxMarks":5,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = 0.18 and x = -1.85","solution":"Using x = [-b ± sqrt(b^2 - 4ac)]/(2a) with a = 3, b = 5 and c = -1: b^2 - 4ac = 25 - 4(3)(-1) = 37, and sqrt(37) = 6.0828. So x = (-5 ± 6.0828)/6, giving x = 0.18 or x = -1.85.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v9::b1","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v9::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0","solution":"At a point of intersection the two y-values are equal, so x^2 - 3x + 4 = 2x - 2. Collecting all the terms on one side gives x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","code":"M1","marks":1,"field":"working","depends":[],"profile":"algorithmic","description":"equates the line and the curve","check":{"type":"containsEquivalentExpression","value":"x^2 - 3x + 4"}},{"kind":"M","code":"M2","marks":1,"field":"working","depends":["M1"],"profile":"algorithmic","description":"collects every term on one side","check":{"type":"containsEquivalentExpression","value":"(x^2 - 3x + 4) - (2x - 2)"}},{"kind":"A","code":"A1","marks":1,"field":"answer","depends":["M2"],"strictDepends":true,"profile":"algorithmic","description":"reaches x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0","check":{"type":"equation","value":"x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0"}}]}},{"id":"p2-q8-v9::b2","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v9::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(2, 2) and (3, 4)","solution":"Factorising, (x - 2)(x - 3) = 0, so x = 2 or x = 3. Substituting into y = 2x - 2 gives y = 2 and y = 4. The points are (2, 2) and (3, 4).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v9::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"34.5","solution":"A bearing is measured clockwise from north, so the northerly component is 45 cos 320° = 34.47. Q is 34.5 km north of P.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v9::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v9::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"28.9","solution":"The easterly component is 45 sin 320° = -28.93, so Q is 28.9 km west of P. Check: 34.5^2 + 28.9^2 gives 45^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v9::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"83.2","solution":"Adding the components of the second leg, R is 79.47 km north and 24.70 km east of P. So PR = sqrt(79.47^2 + 24.70^2) = 83.2 km.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v9::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v9::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"017","solution":"tan(bearing) = east / north = 24.70 / 79.47, so the bearing of R from P is 17.3°, that is 017° to the nearest degree.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v9::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(8, 6)","solution":"\\vec{AB} = \\vec{OB} - \\vec{OA} = (10 - 2, 5 - -1) = (8, 6).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v9::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v9::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10.00","solution":"|\\vec{AB}| = sqrt(8^2 + 6^2) = sqrt(100) = 10.00 units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v9::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(6, 2)","solution":"AC : CB = 1 : 1, so \\vec{AC} = (1/2)\\vec{AB} = (4, 3). Then \\vec{OC} = \\vec{OA} + \\vec{AC} = (6, 2).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v9::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v9::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"not parallel","solution":"\\vec{OC} = (6, 2) and \\vec{AB} = (8, 6). For them to be parallel we would need 6 × 6 = 2 × 8, that is 36 = 16, which is false. So they are not parallel.","criteria":null}}]'::jsonb,false,'draft')
