values ('mathematics','source-scheme-draft-v2','original-v10','[{"id":"p2-q1-v10::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v10::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"7","solution":"(2 2/5 + 1 1/3) = 12/5 + 4/3 = 36/15 + 20/15 = 56/15. (7/10 - 1/6) = 7/10 - 1/6 = 21/30 - 5/30 = 8/15. Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal, so 56/15 ÷ 8/15 = 56/15 × 15/8 = 7.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v10::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v10::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3000.00","solution":"Total parts = 3 + 4 + 5 = 12. One part = 7,200 ÷ 12 = $600.00. Largest share = 5 × 600.00 = $3000.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v10::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v10::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"1200.00","solution":"Smallest share = 3 × 600.00 = $1800.00. Difference = 3000.00 - 1800.00 = $1200.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q1-v10::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q1-v10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"12","solution":"The job needs 6 × 20 = 120 worker-days. With 10 workers this takes 120 ÷ 10 = 12 days.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v10::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v10::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4x + 3y = 41; 2x + 5y = 45","solution":"From the first purchase, 4x + 3y = 41. From the second, 2x + 5y = 45.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v10::b","maxMarks":5,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v10::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"cup $5.00, plate $7.00","solution":"Multiply the first equation by 2 and the second by 4 to eliminate x, or use substitution. Solving gives x = 5 and y = 7. Check: 4(5) + 3(7) = 41 and 2(5) + 5(7) = 45.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q2-v10::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q2-v10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"65","solution":"Total = 6(5) + 5(7) = $65.00.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v10::a","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v10::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"A correct construction of triangle PQR","solution":"Draw PQ = 9 cm and extend the straight line slightly through Q. With centre Q, draw an arc cutting the line at two points, one on each side of Q. Using those two cut points as centres and the same compass radius, draw two arcs to intersect above Q. Join Q to their intersection to construct the perpendicular, giving angle PQR = 90°. With centre Q and radius 5 cm, draw an arc to cut the perpendicular at R. Join P to R. Leave all construction arcs clearly visible.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v10::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v10::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10.3","solution":"By the cosine rule the true length is PR^2 = 9^2 + 5^2 - 2(9)(5)cos 90° = 106.00, so PR = 10.30 cm. A measurement of 10.3 cm is expected.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q3-v10::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q3-v10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"22.5","solution":"Area = 1/2 × PQ × QR × sin(angle PQR) = 1/2 × 9 × 5 × sin 90° = 22.5 cm^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v10::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v10::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"7, 4, 1, -2, -5","solution":"Substituting each value of x in turn: f(-1) = 7; f(0) = 4; f(1) = 1; f(2) = -2; f(3) = -5.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v10::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v10::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"{-5, -2, 1, 4, 7}","solution":"The range is the set of output values: {-5, -2, 1, 4, 7}.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v10::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = 5; not in the domain","solution":"-3x + 4 = -11 gives -3x = -15 and x = 5. This value is not in the given domain.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q4-v10::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q4-v10::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"Yes, one-to-one, because every member of the domain gives a different value of f(x), so no two members map onto the same member of the range","solution":"Every value of x gives a different value of f(x), because the relation is linear with a non-zero gradient, so no two members of the domain map onto the same member of the range. The relation is therefore one-to-one.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","code":"B1","marks":1,"field":"answer","depends":[],"profile":"conceptual","description":"states that the relation is one-to-one","check":{"type":"written","any":["one to one","one-to-one","1-1","yes"],"none":["many to one","many-to-one","not one to one"]}},{"kind":"B","code":"B2","marks":1,"field":"all","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"gives a valid reason","check":{"type":"written","any":["different","distinct","no two","each x","every x","unique","linear","non-zero gradient","not repeated","no repeated","each member of the domain","one output"]}}]}},{"id":"p2-q5-v10::a","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v10::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"21 - 25","solution":"The class 21 - 25 has the highest frequency, 12.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v10::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v10::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"17","solution":"Use the class midpoints 3, 8, 13, 18, 23. Sum of fx = 3(3) + 3(8) + 3(13) + 9(18) + 12(23) = 510. Mean = 510 / 30 = 17 kg.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v10::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3, 6, 9, 18, 30","solution":"Add the frequencies in order: 3, 6, 9, 18, 30.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q5-v10::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q5-v10::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"7/10","solution":"21 of the 30 parcels have a mass greater than 15 kg, so the probability is 21/30 = 7/10.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v10::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v10::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"31.5","solution":"tan 42° = TB / 35, so TB = 35 tan 42° = 31.51 = 31.5 m.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v10::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v10::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"47.1","solution":"cos 42° = 35 / AT, so AT = 35 / cos 42° = 47.10 = 47.1 m.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q6-v10::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q6-v10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"32","solution":"tan(angle) = TB / 50 = 31.51 / 50 = 0.6303, so the angle of elevation is 32.2°, which is 32° to the nearest degree. It is smaller than 42°, as expected, because C is further from the tower.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v10::a","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v10::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"7","solution":"Each term is 7 more than the one before.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v10::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v10::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"7n - 2","solution":"T_n = a + (n - 1)d = 5 + (n - 1)(7) = 7n - 2. Check with n = 1: 7(1) - 2 = 5.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v10::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"96","solution":"T_14 = 5 + (14 - 1)(7) = 96.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v10::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v10::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"810","solution":"S_n = (n/2)[2a + (n - 1)d], so S_15 = (15/2)[2(5) + (15 - 1)(7)] = 810.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q7-v10::e","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q7-v10::e","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"the 20th term","solution":"Set 7n - 2 = 138. Then 7n = 140 and n = 20, so 138 is the 20th term.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v10::a","maxMarks":5,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v10::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = 0.64 and x = -3.14","solution":"Using x = [-b ± sqrt(b^2 - 4ac)]/(2a) with a = 2, b = 5 and c = -4: b^2 - 4ac = 25 - 4(2)(-4) = 57, and sqrt(57) = 7.5498. So x = (-5 ± 7.5498)/4, giving x = 0.64 or x = -3.14.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q8-v10::b1","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v10::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x^2 - 3x - 10 = 0","solution":"At a point of intersection the two y-values are equal, so x^2 + x - 11 = 4x - 1. Collecting all the terms on one side gives x^2 - 3x - 10 = 0.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","code":"M1","marks":1,"field":"working","depends":[],"profile":"algorithmic","description":"equates the line and the curve","check":{"type":"containsEquivalentExpression","value":"x^2 + x - 11"}},{"kind":"M","code":"M2","marks":1,"field":"working","depends":["M1"],"profile":"algorithmic","description":"collects every term on one side","check":{"type":"containsEquivalentExpression","value":"(x^2 + x - 11) - (4x - 1)"}},{"kind":"A","code":"A1","marks":1,"field":"answer","depends":["M2"],"strictDepends":true,"profile":"algorithmic","description":"reaches x^2 - 3x - 10 = 0","check":{"type":"equation","value":"x^2 - 3x - 10 = 0"}}]}},{"id":"p2-q8-v10::b2","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q8-v10::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(-2, -9) and (5, 19)","solution":"Factorising, (x + 2)(x - 5) = 0, so x = -2 or x = 5. Substituting into y = 4x - 1 gives y = -9 and y = 19. The points are (-2, -9) and (5, 19).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v10::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v10::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"45.0","solution":"A bearing is measured clockwise from north, so the northerly component is 90 cos 240° = -45.00. Q is 45.0 km south of P.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v10::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v10::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"77.9","solution":"The easterly component is 90 sin 240° = -77.94, so Q is 77.9 km west of P. Check: 45.0^2 + 77.9^2 gives 90^2.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v10::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"103.0","solution":"Adding the components of the second leg, R is -88.30 km north and -52.94 km east of P. So PR = sqrt(-88.30^2 + -52.94^2) = 103.0 km.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q9-v10::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q9-v10::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"211","solution":"tan(bearing) = east / north = -52.94 / -88.30, so the bearing of R from P is 210.9°, that is 211° to the nearest degree.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v10::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v10::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(9, 6)","solution":"\\vec{AB} = \\vec{OB} - \\vec{OA} = (8 - -1, 8 - 2) = (9, 6).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v10::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v10::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"10.82","solution":"|\\vec{AB}| = sqrt(9^2 + 6^2) = sqrt(117) = 10.82 units.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v10::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(5, 6)","solution":"AC : CB = 2 : 1, so \\vec{AC} = (2/3)\\vec{AB} = (6, 4). Then \\vec{OC} = \\vec{OA} + \\vec{AC} = (5, 6).","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2-q10-v10::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2-q10-v10::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"not parallel","solution":"\\vec{OC} = (5, 6) and \\vec{AB} = (9, 6). For them to be parallel we would need 5 × 6 = 6 × 9, that is 30 = 54, which is false. So they are not parallel.","criteria":null}}]'::jsonb,false,'draft')
