values ('mathematics','source-scheme-draft-v2','p2g','[{"id":"p2g-q1::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q1::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"114/55","solution":"2 3/5 = 13/5, so the numerator is 13/5 - 7/10 = 19/10. The denominator is 3/4 + 1/6 = 11/12. Dividing means multiplying by the reciprocal: 19/10 x 12/11 = 114/55.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"writes the numerator as a single fraction","check":{"type":"contains","value":[1.9]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"writes the denominator as a single fraction","check":{"type":"contains","value":[0.9166666666666666]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the exact value in its lowest terms","check":{"type":"fraction","value":2.0727272727272728,"simplified":true,"requireFraction":true},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q1::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q1::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5600.00","solution":"The discount is 12.5% of $6,400 = $800.00. The cash price is $6,400 - $800.00 = $5,600.00.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"finds 12.5% of $6,400","check":{"type":"contains","value":[800]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the cash price","check":{"type":"numeric","value":5600,"dp":2,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q1::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q1::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"6440.00","solution":"VAT = 15% of $5,600.00 = $840.00. The customer pays $5,600.00 + $840.00 = $6,440.00.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"finds 15% of the cash price","check":{"type":"contains","value":[840]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the amount paid","check":{"type":"numeric","value":6440,"dp":2,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["b1"],"formula":"b1 * 1.15"},"code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q1::c","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q1::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"1135.00","solution":"The hire purchase price is $1,200 + 15 x $425 = $1,200 + $6,375 = $7,575.00. That is $7,575.00 - $6,440.00 = $1,135.00 more.","criteria":[{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the extra amount paid","check":{"type":"numeric","value":1135,"dp":2,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["b2"],"formula":"7575.0 - b2"},"code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q1::d","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q1::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"Cash, because paying by hire purchase costs $1,135 more","solution":"The hire purchase arrangement costs $7,575 in total against $6,440 for cash, so the customer pays $1,135 more by hire purchase and should pay cash.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","code":"B1","marks":1,"field":"answer","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"advises cash and gives the extra cost as the reason","check":{"type":"prose","key":"cash, because hire purchase costs 1135 more","tokens":["cash","more","1135"],"mustHave":["cash"],"forbid":[],"polarity":"positive","quorum":0.5}}]}},{"id":"p2g-q2::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q2::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"12","solution":"Substituting m = 3 and n = -4: the numerator is 4(3)^2 + 3(-4) = 36 - 12 = 24, and the denominator is 2(3) + (-4) = 6 - 4 = 2. So W = 24/2 = 12.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"substitutes m = 3 and n = -4 into the formula","check":{"type":"contains","value":[3,-4]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the value of W","check":{"type":"numeric","value":12,"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q2::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q2::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"6y^2 - 7y - 20","solution":"Multiplying each term in the first bracket by each term in the second: (3y + 4)(2y - 5) = 6y^2 - 15y + 8y - 20. Collecting the two terms in y: 6y^2 - 7y - 20.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"multiplies out to give the four products","check":{"type":"contains","value":[15,8]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the expansion in its simplest form","check":{"type":"expression","value":"6y^2 - 7y - 20","accepted":["6y^2 - 20 - 7y"]},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q2::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q2::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"2(x + 2)(x + 3)","solution":"Take out the common factor 2: 2(x^2 + 5x + 6). Two numbers whose product is 6 and whose sum is 5 are 2 and 3, so 2x^2 + 10x + 12 = 2(x + 2)(x + 3).","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"takes out the common factor 2","check":{"type":"method","any":["common factor 2"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the complete factorisation","check":{"type":"expression","value":"2(x + 2)(x + 3)","accepted":["2(x + 3)(x + 2)"],"requireFactorised":true},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q2::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q2::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x >= -13/4; the smallest integer value of x is -3","solution":"7x + 4 ≥ 3x - 9. Collecting the terms in x on one side and the numbers on the other: 4x ≥ -13. Dividing both sides by 4: x ≥ -13/4. Since -13/4 lies between -4 and -3, the smallest integer value of x that satisfies the inequality is -3.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"collects the terms in x on one side","check":{"type":"contains","value":[4,-13]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"solves the inequality","check":{"type":"inequality","value":"x >= -13/4"},"field":"all","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"states the smallest integer value of x","check":{"type":"numeric","value":-3,"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B1"}]}},{"id":"p2g-q3::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"A(-5, 6) and B(3, 2) correctly plotted","solution":"A(-5, 6) is 5 units to the left of the y-axis and 6 units above the x-axis. B(3, 2) is 3 units to the right of the y-axis and 2 units above the x-axis. Each point is marked where those two grid lines cross.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2g-q3::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q3::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(-1, 4)","solution":"The midpoint of AB is ((-5) + (3))/2 for the x-coordinate and ((6) + (2))/2 for the y-coordinate. Now (-5) + (3) = -2 and (6) + (2) = 8, so the midpoint of AB is (-1, 4).","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"adds the two x-coordinates and the two y-coordinates, and halves each sum","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"contains","value":[-2,8]},{"type":"coordinate","value":[-1,4],"tolerance":0.000001}]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the coordinates of the midpoint","check":{"type":"coordinate","value":[-1,4],"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q3::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-1/2","solution":"The gradient of AB is (the change in y)/(the change in x). The change in y is (2) - (6) = -4 and the change in x is (3) - (-5) = 8, so the gradient of AB is -4/8 = -1/2.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses gradient = (y2 - y1)/(x2 - x1)","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"contains","value":[-4,8]},{"type":"numeric","value":-0.5,"tolerance":0.000001}]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the gradient of AB","check":{"type":"numeric","value":-0.5,"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q3::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q3::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"y = (-1/2)x + 7/2","solution":"The gradient is m = -1/2. Substituting m = -1/2 and the point A(-5, 6) into y = mx + c gives (6) = (-1/2)(-5) + c, that is (6) = 5/2 + c, so c = (6) - (5/2) = 7/2. The equation of the line AB is y = (-1/2)x + 7/2.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"substitutes the gradient and the coordinates of a point on the line into y = mx + c","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"method","any":["y = mx + c","substituting"]},{"type":"equation","value":"y = (-1/2)x + 7/2"}]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the value of the intercept c","check":{"type":"contains","value":[3.5]},"field":"all","ecf":{"uses":["c"],"formula":"(6) - c * (-5)"},"code":"A1","depends":["M1"]},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the equation of AB in the form y = mx + c","check":{"type":"equation","value":"y = (-1/2)x + 7/2"},"field":"answer","code":"A2","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q4::a1","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q4::a1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"the perpendicular bisector of AB, with the construction arcs shown","solution":"Open the compasses to more than half of AB. With centre A draw arcs above and below AB; with the SAME radius and centre B draw two more, cutting the first pair. Rule the line through the two crossing points. That line is the perpendicular bisector of AB, and the arcs must be left on the page.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2g-q4::a2","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q4::a2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4","solution":"The perpendicular bisector of AB cuts AB at its midpoint, so AM = (1/2) x 8 = 4 cm.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"the length of AM","check":{"type":"numeric","value":4,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B1"}]}},{"id":"p2g-q4::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4.3","solution":"M is the midpoint of AB, so KM is measured with the ruler from K to M and is 4.3 cm. (A check by Pythagoras'' theorem: K is 2.5 cm to the right of M and 3.5 cm above it, so KM = sqrt(18.5) = 4.30 cm.) A reading within 0.5 cm earns the first mark and a reading within 0.25 cm earns the second.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"a reading within 0.5 cm of the correct value","check":{"type":"numeric","value":4.301162633521313,"tolerance":0.5},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B1"},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"the value correct to within 0.25 cm","check":{"type":"numeric","value":4.301162633521313,"tolerance":0.25},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B2"}]}},{"id":"p2g-q4::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q4::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"129","solution":"Area of the trapezium = (1/2) x (20 + 12) x 9 = (1/2) x 32 x 9 = 144 cm^2. Area of the triangular pond = (1/2) x 6 x 5 = 15 cm^2. Area remaining = 144 - 15 = 129 cm^2.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses area of a trapezium = (1/2) x (a + b) x h","check":{"type":"contains","value":[144]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"finds the area of the triangle as (1/2) x base x height","check":{"type":"contains","value":[15]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the area that remains","check":{"type":"numeric","value":129,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q5::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"25.5, 35.5, 45.5; 459, 461.5, 273","solution":"The mid-interval value is the mean of the class boundaries, and f x is the frequency times that value: (21 + 30)/2 = 25.5, 18 x 25.5 = 459; (31 + 40)/2 = 35.5, 13 x 35.5 = 461.5; (41 + 50)/2 = 45.5, 6 x 45.5 = 273.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2g-q5::b","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"21 - 30","solution":"The class 21 - 30 has the highest frequency, 18.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"the modal class","check":{"type":"set","value":[21,30],"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B1"}]}},{"id":"p2g-q5::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"27.1","solution":"Use the mid-interval values 5.5, 15.5, 25.5, 35.5, 45.5. The sum of f x is 22 + 139.5 + 459 + 461.5 + 273 = 1355. The estimated mean is 1355/50 = 27.1.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses the mid-interval values","check":{"type":"contains","value":[45.5]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the estimated mean","check":{"type":"numeric","value":27.1,"dp":1,"tolerance":0.06},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q5::c2","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q5::c2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"The data is grouped, so the midpoint of each class is used in place of the actual values, which are not known","solution":"Once the values are grouped, the individual values are no longer recorded. The calculation uses the midpoint of each class as though every value in that class were the midpoint, so the answer is an estimate.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","code":"B1","marks":1,"field":"answer","depends":[],"profile":"reasoning","description":"says the actual values are unknown because the data is grouped","check":{"type":"prose","key":"the data is grouped so midpoints are used instead of the actual values","tokens":["grouped","midpoint","actual","values","not","known"],"mustHave":[],"forbid":[],"polarity":"positive","quorum":0.25}}]}},{"id":"p2g-q5::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q5::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"19/50","solution":"19 of the 50 values are at least 31, so the probability is 19/50.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"finds how many are at least 31","check":{"type":"contains","value":[19]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the probability in its lowest terms","check":{"type":"fraction","value":0.38,"simplified":true,"requireFraction":true},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q6::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"90","solution":"OA and OB are radii of the same circle, so OA = OB and triangle OAB is isosceles. Hence angle OBA = angle OAB = 45°. The angles of a triangle add up to 180°, so y = 180 - 45 - 45 = 90°.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses OA = OB, so angle OBA = angle OAB","check":{"type":"method","any":["isosceles","radii","radius"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the size of angle AOB","check":{"type":"numeric","value":90,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q6::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"45","solution":"Angle AOB at the centre and angle ACB at the circumference both stand on the same arc AB. The angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference, so x = 90° / 2 = 45°.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses the angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference","check":{"type":"method","any":["twice the angle at the circumference","angle at the centre"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the size of angle ACB","check":{"type":"numeric","value":45,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["a"],"formula":"a / 2"},"code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q6::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"The angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference when both angles stand on the same arc AB, so angle ACB is half of angle AOB, giving x = 45 degrees.","solution":"Angle AOB and angle ACB both stand on the arc AB, one at the centre and one at the circumference. The theorem the angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference standing on the same arc gives angle ACB = 90° / 2 = 45°. Naming the theorem earns 1 mark and saying that the two angles stand on the same arc AB earns the second.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"names the theorem: the angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference","check":{"type":"written","id":"theorem","description":"names the theorem: the angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference","any":["angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference","twice the angle at the circumference","centre is twice"]},"field":"answer","code":"B1"},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"states that the two angles stand on the same arc","check":{"type":"written","id":"arc","description":"states that the two angles stand on the same arc","any":["same arc","same segment","arc ab"]},"field":"answer","code":"B2"}]}},{"id":"p2g-q6::d","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q6::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"22","solution":"The angle of the sector at the centre is 90°, so the minor arc AB is 90/360 = 1/4 of the circumference. Arc length = (90/360) x 2 x π x r = (1/4) x 2 x (22/7) x 14 = (1/4) x 88 = 22 cm.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses arc length = (angle/360) x 2 x pi x r","check":{"type":"method","any":["/360","arc length"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"substitutes r = 14 and pi = 22/7","check":{"type":"contains","value":[88]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the length of the arc","check":{"type":"numeric","value":22,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["a"],"formula":"a * 0.24444444444444444"},"code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q7::a","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"20, 30, 110, n(n + 1)","solution":"The number of dots in Figure n is n(n + 1). Figure 4 has 20 dots and Figure 5 has 30 dots, each found by continuing the pattern or by using the rule. Figure 10 has 110 dots. In Figure n there are n(n + 1) dots, which checks against the table: for n = 3 it gives 12.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2g-q7::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"930","solution":"Using the rule n(n + 1) from (a) with n = 30: 30 x 31 = 930. So Figure 30 has 930 dots.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"substitutes n = 30 into the rule for Figure n","check":{"type":"contains","value":[31]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the number of dots in Figure 30","check":{"type":"numeric","value":930,"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q7::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"23","solution":"Set the rule equal to 552: n(n + 1) = 552. Expanding the left-hand side gives n^2 + n = 552, that is n^2 + n - 552 = 0. Factorising, (n + 24)(n - 23) = 0, so n = -24 or n = 23. A figure number must be a positive whole number, so the figure is Figure 23. Check: 23 x 24 = 552.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"writes the equation n(n + 1) = 552","check":{"type":"contains","value":[552]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"writes it as a quadratic equation equal to zero","check":{"type":"method","any":["n^2 + n - 552 = 0"]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"solves the quadratic equation","check":{"type":"method","any":["(n + 24)(n - 23)","factoris","quadratic formula"]},"field":"all","code":"M3"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the figure number, rejecting the negative root","check":{"type":"numeric","value":23,"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M3"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q8::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"-5, -5","solution":"when x = -3, y = (-3)^2 + 2(-3) - 8 = -5; when x = 1, y = (1)^2 + 2(1) - 8 = -5.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2g-q8::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q8::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"the points (-5, 7) to (3, 7) joined by a smooth curve","solution":"Plot the seven points from the table and join them with a single smooth curve. Do not join them with straight lines.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2g-q8::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q8::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(-1, -9)","solution":"The curve turns at its lowest point, where x = -1 and y = -9. The minimum point is (-1, -9).","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"identifies the turning point of the curve","check":{"type":"contains","value":[-1]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the coordinates of the minimum","check":{"type":"coordinate","value":[-1,-9],"tolerance":0.3},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"],"captureIndex":0}]}},{"id":"p2g-q8::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q8::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = -4 and x = 2","solution":"The curve crosses the x axis where y = 0, at x = -4 and x = 2.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"reads where the curve crosses the x axis","check":{"type":"method","any":["x axis","y = 0","crosses"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"both values of x","check":{"type":"set","value":[-4,2],"tolerance":0.3},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q8::e","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q8::e","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = -1","solution":"The axis of symmetry is the vertical line through the minimum point, so its equation is x = -1.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"refers to the vertical line through the minimum","check":{"type":"method","any":["axis of symmetry","vertical","minimum"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the equation of the axis of symmetry","check":{"type":"equation","value":"x = -1"},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["c"],"formula":"c","template":"x = {v}"},"code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q9::a","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"131.8","solution":"The bearing of P from Q is 62 + 180 = 242°, so angle PQR = 242 - 137 = 105°. By the cosine rule, PR^2 = PQ^2 + QR^2 - 2(PQ)(QR) cos PQR = 70^2 + 95^2 - 2(70)(95) cos 105° = 4900 + 9025 + 3442.2933 = 17367.2933. So PR = sqrt(17367.2933) = 131.7850 = 131.8 km, correct to 1 decimal place.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"finds angle PQR = 105 degrees from the bearings","check":{"type":"contains","value":[105]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses the cosine rule","check":{"type":"method","any":["cosine rule","cos"]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"substitutes 70, 95 and 105 correctly","check":{"type":"contains","value":[70,95,105]},"field":"all","code":"M3"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"PR = 131.8 km","check":{"type":"numeric","value":131.7850268424434,"dp":1,"tolerance":0.06},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M3"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q9::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q9::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"44.1","solution":"By the sine rule, sin(angle QPR)/QR = sin(angle PQR)/PR, that is sin(angle QPR)/95 = sin 105°/131.7850. So sin(angle QPR) = 95 x sin 105° / 131.7850 = 0.696308, giving angle QPR = 44.13 = 44.1°. Angle PQR is obtuse, so angle QPR must be acute and this is the required value.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses the sine rule","check":{"type":"method","any":["sine rule","sin"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"substitutes 95, 105 and PR correctly","check":{"type":"contains","value":[95,105,131.785]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"angle QPR = 44.1 degrees","check":{"type":"numeric","value":44.13153068806846,"dp":1,"tolerance":0.06},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["a"],"formula":"asin(95*sin(105)/a)"},"code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q9::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"106","solution":"The bearing of Q from P is 062°, and R lies clockwise of Q when viewed from P, so the bearing of R from P is the bearing of Q from P plus angle QPR. That is 62 + 44.1 = 106.1°, which is 106° as a three-figure bearing correct to the nearest degree.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"bearing of R from P = bearing of Q from P + angle QPR","check":{"type":"method","any":["bearing of q from p"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"adds angle QPR to 062 degrees","check":{"type":"contains","value":[62,44.1]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"106 degrees","check":{"type":"numeric","value":106.13153068806847,"dp":0,"tolerance":0.51},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["b"],"formula":"62 + b"},"code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q9::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q9::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3211.7","solution":"Area = (1/2)(PQ)(QR) sin PQR = (1/2) x 70 x 95 x sin 105° = 3325 x sin 105° = 3211.7034 = 3211.7 km^2, correct to 1 decimal place.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses (1/2)ab sin C with 70, 95 and 105","check":{"type":"contains","value":[70,95,105]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"area = 3211.7 km^2","check":{"type":"numeric","value":3211.703372411152,"dp":1,"tolerance":0.06},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q10::k","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q10::k","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5","solution":"det M = (2)(1) - (-3)(1) = 2 - (-3) = 5.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses det M = ad - bc","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"contains","value":[2,-3]},{"type":"contains","value":[2,3]},{"type":"contains","value":[5]},{"type":"method","any":["(2)(1) - (-3)(1)","2(1) - -3(1)","2 x 1 - -3 x 1","2*1 - -3*1","ad - bc","ad-bc"]}]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the determinant","check":{"type":"numeric","value":5,"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q10::a2","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q10::a2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1/5)[[1, 3], [-1, 2]]","solution":"For M = [[a, b], [c, d]], M^-1 = (1/det M)[[d, -b], [-c, a]]. Interchange the entries on the leading diagonal, change the sign of the other two, and divide by the determinant: M^-1 = (1/5)[[1, 3], [-1, 2]] = [[1/5, 3/5], [-1/5, 2/5]].","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"interchanges the leading diagonal entries and changes the sign of the other two","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"contains","value":[1,3,-1,2]},{"type":"contains","value":[0.2,0.6,-0.2,0.4]}]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"divides by the determinant","check":{"type":"contains","value":[0.2,-0.2],"needAll":false,"tolerance":0.005},"field":"all","ecf":{"uses":["k"],"formula":"1/k"},"code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the inverse matrix","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"matrix","value":[[0.2,0.6],[-0.2,0.4]],"tolerance":0.005},{"type":"contains","value":[0.2,1,3,-1,2]}]},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2g-q10::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q10::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"[[2, -3], [1, 1]] [[x], [y]] = [[5], [5]]","solution":"The coefficients of x and y form the matrix M = [[2, -3], [1, 1]], the unknowns form the column matrix X = [[x], [y]], and the constants form the column matrix C = [[5], [5]]. The pair of equations is therefore [[2, -3], [1, 1]] [[x], [y]] = [[5], [5]].","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"the matrix of coefficients","check":{"type":"contains","value":[2,-3,1,1]},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B1"},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"the column matrix of unknowns","check":{"type":"method","any":["[[x], [y]]","[[x],[y]]","(x, y)"]},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B2"},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"the column matrix of constants","check":{"type":"contains","value":[5,5]},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B3"}]}},{"id":"p2g-q10::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2g-q10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = 4, y = 1","solution":"Multiplying both sides of M X = C on the left by M^-1 gives X = M^-1 C = (1/5)[[1, 3], [-1, 2]] [[5], [5]] = (1/5)[[(1)(5) + (3)(5)], [(-1)(5) + (2)(5)]] = (1/5)[[20], [5]] = [[4], [1]]. So x = 4 and y = 1. Check: 2(4) + (-3)(1) = 5.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"multiplies both sides by the inverse matrix","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"method","any":["M^-1 C","M^-1","inverse"]},{"type":"contains","value":[4,1]}]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"multiplies the inverse by the column of constants","check":{"type":"contains","value":[20,5]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the value of x","check":{"type":"contains","value":[4]},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["k"],"formula":"(20)/k"},"depends":["M1"],"code":"A1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the value of y","check":{"type":"contains","value":[1]},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["k"],"formula":"(5)/k"},"depends":["M1"],"code":"A2"}]}}]'::jsonb,false,'draft')
on conflict(subject_id,rubric_version,paper_id) do nothing;
insert into spark_grading_private.rubrics_v2(subject_id,rubric_version,paper_id,criteria,active,verification_status)
values ('mathematics','source-scheme-draft-v2','p2h','[{"id":"p2h-q1::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q1::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"97/14","solution":"3 1/6 = 19/6, so the numerator is 19/6 + 7/8 = 97/24. The denominator is 5/6 - 1/4 = 7/12. Dividing means multiplying by the reciprocal: 97/24 x 12/7 = 97/14.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"writes the numerator as a single fraction","check":{"type":"contains","value":[4.041666666666667]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"writes the denominator as a single fraction","check":{"type":"contains","value":[0.5833333333333334]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the exact value in its lowest terms","check":{"type":"fraction","value":6.928571428571429,"simplified":true,"requireFraction":true},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q1::b1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q1::b1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4320.00","solution":"640 x 6.75 = TT$4,320.00.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"multiplies by the exchange rate","check":{"type":"method","any":["x 6.75","exchange rate","640"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the amount in TT dollars","check":{"type":"numeric","value":4320,"dp":2,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q1::b2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q1::b2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"4280.00","solution":"TT$4,320.00 - TT$40 = TT$4,280.00.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"subtracts the fee from the amount converted","check":{"type":"contains","value":[40]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the amount received","check":{"type":"numeric","value":4280,"dp":2,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["b1"],"formula":"b1 - 40.0"},"code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q1::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q1::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"14400.00","solution":"I = PRT/100 = (12,000 x 5 x 4)/100 = TT$2,400.00. The total amount is 12,000 + 2,400.00 = TT$14,400.00.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses I = PRT/100","check":{"type":"contains","value":[2400]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the total amount","check":{"type":"numeric","value":14400,"dp":2,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q2::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q2::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3(x - 3)/(x + 5)","solution":"Factorising the numerator: 3x^2 - 27 = 3(x + 3)(x - 3). Factorising the denominator: x^2 + 8x + 15 = (x + 3)(x + 5). The common factor (x + 3) cancels, leaving 3(x - 3)/(x + 5).","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"factorises the numerator","check":{"type":"method","any":["3(x + 3)(x - 3)"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"factorises the denominator","check":{"type":"method","any":["(x + 3)(x + 5)"]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"cancels the common factor and gives the fraction in its lowest terms","check":{"type":"expression","value":"3(x - 3)/(x + 5)","accepted":["3(x-3)/(x+5)","(3x - 9)/(x + 5)"]},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q2::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q2::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x = 3, y = 3/2","solution":"The coefficient of y is the same in both equations. Subtracting x + 2y = 6 from 4x + 2y = 15 eliminates y: 3x = 9, so x = 3. Substituting x = 3 into 4x + 2y = 15 gives 12 + 2y = 15, so 2y = 3 and y = 3/2.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"eliminates one of the variables","check":{"type":"method","any":["eliminates y","eliminates x"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the value of x","check":{"type":"equation","value":"x = 3"},"field":"all","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"substitutes back to find the second variable","check":{"type":"contains","value":[12]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the value of y","check":{"type":"equation","value":"y = 3/2"},"field":"all","code":"A2","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q2::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q2::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"a = 2A/h - b","solution":"Multiplying both sides by 2: 2A = h(a + b). Dividing both sides by h: 2A/h = a + b. Subtracting b from both sides: a = 2A/h - b.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"carries out a correct first step in the rearrangement","check":{"type":"method","any":["2A = h(a + b)"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"a as the subject","check":{"type":"equation","value":"a = 2A/h - b"},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q3::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q3::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"8","solution":"Every one of the 40 students is counted exactly once in the Venn diagram, so (24 - x) + x + (18 - x) + 6 = 40. This simplifies to 48 - x = 40, so x = 48 - 40 = 8. So 8 students study both Geography and History.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"forms an equation in x from the four regions of the Venn diagram","check":{"type":"method","any":["24 - x","24 + 18 - x","48 - x"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"simplifies the equation","check":{"type":"contains","value":[48]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the number who study both Geography and History","check":{"type":"numeric","value":8,"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"A1"}]}},{"id":"p2h-q3::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q3::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"26","solution":"The number who study Geography only is 24 - 8 = 16, and the number who study History only is 18 - 8 = 10. So the number who study exactly one of the two subjects is 16 + 10 = 26.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"subtracts the number who study both from each of 24 and 18","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"method","any":["24 - ","18 - "]},{"type":"contains","value":[16,10]},{"type":"contains","value":[26]}]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the number who study exactly one of the two subjects","check":{"type":"numeric","value":26,"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["a"],"formula":"42 - 2 * a"},"code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q3::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q3::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3/20","solution":"6 of the 40 students study neither Geography nor History, and each student is equally likely to be chosen. So P(neither) = 6/40 = 3/20.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses P(neither) = (the number who study neither)/(the total number of students)","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"contains","value":[6,40]},{"type":"contains","value":[0.15]}]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the probability in its lowest terms","check":{"type":"fraction","value":0.15,"simplified":true,"requireFraction":true},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q3::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q3::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"The shaded region represents the students who study History only, that is, the students who study History but not Geography.","solution":"The shading covers the part of the History circle that lies outside the Geography circle, so it is the set of students who study History but do not study Geography - the students who study History only. Naming History earns 1 mark and making it clear that these students do not study Geography earns the second.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"says that the students study History","check":{"type":"written","id":"subject","description":"says that the students study History","any":["history"]},"field":"answer","code":"B1"},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"makes it clear that they do not study Geography","check":{"type":"written","id":"excludes","description":"makes it clear that they do not study Geography","any":["history only","but not geography","do not study geography","not study geography"]},"field":"answer","code":"B2"}]}},{"id":"p2h-q4::a1","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q4::a1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"the perpendicular bisector of AB through M, with the construction arcs shown","solution":"Open the compasses to more than half of AB, that is to more than 3.5 cm. With centre A draw arcs above and below AB; with the SAME radius and centre B draw two more to cut them. Rule the line through the two crossing points. It cuts AB at the midpoint M and makes an angle of 90° with AB. The arcs must be left on the page.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2h-q4::a2","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q4::a2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"the bisector of angle TMB drawn from M, with the arc at M and the two equal arcs from where it cuts MT and MB shown","solution":"With centre M draw an arc cutting MT and MB. From each of those two crossing points, with the same radius, draw an arc so that the two arcs cross. Rule the line from M through that crossing point. This mark is for the arcs: an angle measured with a protractor earns nothing here.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2h-q4::b","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q4::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"45","solution":"MT is perpendicular to AB, so angle TMB = 90°. The bisector halves it, so angle TMR = 90/2 = 45°.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"the size of the constructed angle","check":{"type":"numeric","value":45,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B1"}]}},{"id":"p2h-q4::c1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q4::c1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"0.72","solution":"Volume of a cuboid = length x width x height = 1.2 x 0.8 x 0.75 = 0.96 x 0.75 = 0.72 m^3.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"multiplies length by width by height","check":{"type":"contains","value":[0.96]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the volume of the tank","check":{"type":"numeric","value":0.72,"tolerance":0.0011},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q4::c2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q4::c2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"720","solution":"0.72 m^3 = 0.72 x 1000 litres = 720 litres.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"multiplies the volume in m^3 by 1000","check":{"type":"method","any":["1000"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the capacity in litres","check":{"type":"numeric","value":720,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["c1"],"formula":"c1 * 1000"},"code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q5::a","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q5::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"20, 40, 52, 60","solution":"Add each frequency to the running total: 6 + 14 = 20, 20 + 20 = 40, 40 + 12 = 52, 52 + 8 = 60.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2h-q5::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q5::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"the points (10, 6), (20, 20), (30, 40), (40, 52), (50, 60) joined by a smooth curve","solution":"Plot the cumulative frequency at the upper boundary of each class: (10, 6), (20, 20), (30, 40), (40, 52), (50, 60), then join them with a smooth curve.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2h-q5::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q5::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"25","solution":"The median is the 30th value. Reading across from 30 on the cumulative frequency axis to the curve and down to the horizontal axis gives approximately 25 minutes.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"reads across from 30 on the cumulative frequency axis","check":{"type":"contains","value":[30]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the median","check":{"type":"numeric","value":25,"tolerance":2.5},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q5::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q5::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"2/3","solution":"20 of the 60 values are 20 minutes or less, so 60 - 20 = 40 are more than 20 minutes. The probability is 40/60 = 2/3.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"finds the number greater than 20 minutes","check":{"type":"contains","value":[40]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the probability in its lowest terms","check":{"type":"fraction","value":0.6666666666666666,"simplified":true,"requireFraction":true},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q6::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q6::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"144","solution":"The 10 exterior angles of the polygon add up to 360°, so each exterior angle is 360°/10 = 36°. An interior angle and its exterior angle lie on a straight line, so x = 180 - 36 = 144°.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses exterior angle = 360/10","check":{"type":"contains","value":[36]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses interior angle = 180 - exterior angle","check":{"type":"contains","value":[180]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the interior angle of the regular decagon","check":{"type":"numeric","value":144,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q6::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q6::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"112","solution":"y and the angle of 112° are corresponding angles between the parallel lines PQ and RS, so they are equal. y = 112.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"identifies the pair as corresponding angles","check":{"type":"method","any":["corresponding"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the value of y","check":{"type":"numeric","value":112,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q6::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q6::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"y and the angle of 112 degrees are corresponding angles between the parallel lines PQ and RS, so the two angles are equal.","solution":"PQ is parallel to RS. The angle marked y and the angle of 112° are corresponding angles, and corresponding angles between parallel lines are equal. Naming them as corresponding angles earns 1 mark and saying that the lines PQ and RS are parallel earns the second.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"names the angles as corresponding angles","check":{"type":"written","id":"name","description":"names the angles as corresponding angles","any":["corresponding"],"none":["alternate","co-interior"]},"field":"answer","code":"B1"},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"says that PQ and RS are parallel","check":{"type":"written","id":"parallel","description":"says that PQ and RS are parallel","any":["parallel"]},"field":"answer","code":"B2"}]}},{"id":"p2h-q6::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q6::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"20","solution":"Each exterior angle is 180 - 162 = 18°. The exterior angles add up to 360°, so the number of sides is 360/18 = 20.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"finds the exterior angle as 180 - the interior angle","check":{"type":"contains","value":[18]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the number of sides","check":{"type":"numeric","value":20,"tolerance":0.011},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q7::a","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q7::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"5, 13, 11, 31","solution":"Each new square adds one more vertical stick, so Figure 4 has 5 vertical sticks, and it adds 3 sticks to the total, so Figure 4 uses 13 sticks in all. Figure 10 is too long to draw, so use the rules: it has 10 + 1 = 11 vertical sticks and 3 x 10 + 1 = 31 sticks altogether.","criteria":null}},{"id":"p2h-q7::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q7::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"3n + 1","solution":"Figure n has 2n horizontal sticks, n along the top and n along the bottom, together with n + 1 vertical sticks, so the total is 2n + n + 1 = 3n + 1 sticks. Checking against the table, n = 3 gives 10 and n = 4 gives 13.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"shows how the total number of sticks is built up in Figure n","check":{"type":"contains","value":[3]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the expression for the total number of sticks","check":{"type":"expression","value":"3n + 1","accepted":["2n + (n + 1)","n + 2n + 1"]},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q7::c","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q7::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"33","solution":"The total number of sticks in Figure n is 3n + 1. So 3n + 1 = 100, giving 3n = 99 and n = 33. The figure is Figure 33. Check: 3 x 33 + 1 = 99 + 1 = 100.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"writes the equation 3n + 1 = 100 for the total number of sticks","check":{"type":"contains","value":[99]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the figure number","check":{"type":"numeric","value":33,"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q7::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q7::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"The total number of sticks in Figure n is 3n + 1, which is always one more than a multiple of 3. If 3n + 1 = 51 then 3n = 50 and n = 50/3, which is not a whole number, so no figure in the sequence is made from exactly 51 sticks.","solution":"The totals are 4, 7, 10, 13, and so on, each one more than a multiple of 3, because Figure n uses 3n + 1 sticks. Saying that the total is 3n + 1, one more than a multiple of 3, or writing the equation 3n + 1 = 51, earns 1 mark. Showing that this gives 3n = 50 and n = 50/3, which is not a whole number, earns the second.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"forms 3n + 1 = 51, or states that the total is always one more than a multiple of 3","check":{"type":"written","id":"form","description":"forms 3n + 1 = 51, or states that the total is always one more than a multiple of 3","any":["3n + 1 = 51","one more than a multiple of 3","multiple of 3"]},"field":"answer","code":"B1"},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"shows that n would not be a whole number","check":{"type":"written","id":"why","description":"shows that n would not be a whole number","any":["not a whole number","not an integer","50/3"]},"field":"answer","code":"B2"}]}},{"id":"p2h-q8::a","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q8::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"x + y <= 24; 3x + 2y <= 60","solution":"At most 24 in total gives x + y ≤ 24. The second condition gives 3x + 2y ≤ 60.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":2,"description":"the first inequality","check":{"type":"allOf","options":[{"type":"inequality","value":"x + y <= 24"}]},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B1"},{"kind":"B","marks":2,"description":"the second inequality","check":{"type":"allOf","options":[{"type":"inequality","value":"3x + 2y <= 60"}]},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"B2"}]}},{"id":"p2h-q8::b","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q8::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"P = 9x + 7y","solution":"Each of the x chairs earns $9 and each of the y tables earns $7, so P = 9x + 7y.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses $9 for each of the x chairs","check":{"type":"contains","value":[9]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the expression for the profit","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"equation","value":"P = 9x + 7y"},{"type":"expression","value":"9x + 7y"}]},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q8::c","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q8::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"$168, $192, $180","solution":"Substitute each vertex into P = 9x + 7y: at (0, 24), P = 9(0) + 7(24) = $168; at (12, 12), P = 9(12) + 7(12) = $192; at (20, 0), P = 9(20) + 7(0) = $180.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"substitutes the vertices into P = 9x + 7y","check":{"type":"contains","value":[168]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"evaluates the profit at every vertex","check":{"type":"contains","value":[192]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":2,"description":"all three profits","check":{"type":"set","value":[168,192,180],"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q8::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q8::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"12 chairs and 12 tables, giving a profit of $192","solution":"The greatest of the profits is $192, at the vertex (12, 12). So 12 chairs and 12 tables should be made.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"selects the vertex giving the greatest profit","check":{"type":"contains","value":[192]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"12 chairs and 12 tables","check":{"type":"set","value":[12,12,192],"tolerance":0.000001},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q9::a","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q9::a","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"28.1","solution":"Triangle TBA is right-angled at B, so tan 32° = TB/AB = TB/45. Therefore TB = 45 x tan 32° = 28.1191 = 28.1 m, correct to 1 decimal place.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses tan = opposite/adjacent in triangle TBA","check":{"type":"method","any":["tan"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"substitutes to give TB = 45 tan 32","check":{"type":"contains","value":[45,32]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"TB = 28.1 m","check":{"type":"numeric","value":28.119120835919738,"dp":1,"tolerance":0.06},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q9::b","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q9::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"36.7","solution":"Triangle TBC is right-angled at B, so tan 19° = TB/CB, which gives CB = TB / tan 19°. So CB = 28.1191 / tan 19° = 81.66 m. Since A lies between C and B, AC = CB - AB = 81.66 - 45 = 36.66 = 36.7 m, correct to 1 decimal place.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses tan 19 = TB/CB in triangle TBC","check":{"type":"method","any":["tan"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"rearranges to CB = TB / tan 19","check":{"type":"contains","value":[19,28.1191]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"CB = 81.66 m and AC = CB - 45","check":{"type":"contains","value":[81.66,45]},"field":"all","code":"M3"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"AC = 36.7 m","check":{"type":"numeric","value":36.663856602358976,"dp":1,"tolerance":0.06},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["a"],"formula":"a/tan(19) - 45"},"code":"A1","depends":["M3"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q9::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q9::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"25.1","solution":"The angle of depression of D from T is equal to the angle of elevation of T from D, which is angle TDB. Triangle TBD is right-angled at B, with TB = 28.1191 m and BD = 60 m, so tan(angle TDB) = TB/BD = 0.4687. So angle TDB = 25.11 = 25.1°, and the angle of depression of D from T is 25.1°, correct to 1 decimal place.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses tan(angle TDB) = TB/BD in triangle TBD","check":{"type":"method","any":["tan"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"substitutes TB and BD = 60 correctly","check":{"type":"contains","value":[28.1191,60]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"angle of depression = 25.1 degrees","check":{"type":"numeric","value":25.11023188762961,"dp":1,"tolerance":0.06},"field":"answer","ecf":{"uses":["a"],"formula":"atan(a/60)"},"code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q9::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q9::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"The horizontal line drawn through T is parallel to the level ground AB, and AT is a transversal cutting both of them. The angle of elevation of T from A and the angle of depression of A from T are therefore alternate angles between parallel lines, and alternate angles are equal.","solution":"The angle of elevation is measured at A from the horizontal ground AB up to AT, and the angle of depression is measured at T from the horizontal line through T down to TA. The horizontal line through T is parallel to AB because both are horizontal, and AT is a transversal cutting this pair of parallel lines. The two angles are alternate angles (Z angles) between the parallel lines, so they are equal.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"states that the horizontal line through T is parallel to the ground AB","check":{"type":"written","id":"r1","description":"states that the horizontal line through T is parallel to the ground AB","any":["parallel"]},"field":"answer","code":"B1"},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"identifies the two angles as alternate angles, which are equal","check":{"type":"written","id":"r2","description":"identifies the two angles as alternate angles, which are equal","any":["alternate","z angles"]},"field":"answer","code":"B2"}]}},{"id":"p2h-q10::a1","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q10::a1","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"q - p","solution":"\\vec{PQ} = \\vec{PO} + \\vec{OQ} = -p + q = q - p.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses \\vec{PQ} = \\vec{PO} + \\vec{OQ}","check":{"type":"method","any":["\\vec{PO} + \\vec{OQ}","PO + OQ","-p + q","q - p"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the expression for \\vec{PQ}","check":{"type":"expression","value":"q - p","accepted":["-p + q"]},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q10::a2","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q10::a2","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1/2)q - p","solution":"T is the midpoint of OQ, so \\vec{OT} = (1/2)q. Then \\vec{PT} = \\vec{PO} + \\vec{OT} = -p + (1/2)q = (1/2)q - p.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses \\vec{OT} = (1/2)q","check":{"type":"method","any":["\\vec{OT} = (1/2)q","(1/2)q","q/2","0.5q","1/2 q","(q - 2p)"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the expression for \\vec{PT}","check":{"type":"expression","value":"(1/2)q - p","accepted":["-p + (1/2)q","(q - 2p)/2"]},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M1"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q10::b","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q10::b","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"(1/2)q - (1/2)p","solution":"S is the midpoint of OP, so \\vec{OS} = (1/2)p, and \\vec{OT} = (1/2)q. Then \\vec{ST} = \\vec{SO} + \\vec{OT} = -(1/2)p + (1/2)q = (1/2)(q - p).","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"writes \\vec{OS} = (1/2)p and \\vec{OT} = (1/2)q","check":{"type":"method","any":["\\vec{OS} = (1/2)p","(1/2)p","p/2","0.5p","(1/2)(q - p)","(q - p)/2"]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses \\vec{ST} = \\vec{SO} + \\vec{OT}","check":{"type":"method","any":["\\vec{SO} + \\vec{OT}","\\vec{OT} - \\vec{OS}","SO + OT","(1/2)q - (1/2)p","(1/2)(q - p)","(q - p)/2","0.5q - 0.5p"]},"field":"all","code":"M2"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the simplified expression for \\vec{ST}","check":{"type":"expression","value":"(1/2)q - (1/2)p","accepted":["(1/2)(q - p)","(q - p)/2"]},"field":"answer","code":"A1","depends":["M2"]}]}},{"id":"p2h-q10::c","maxMarks":3,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q10::c","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"\\vec{ST} = (1/2)(q - p) = (1/2)\\vec{PQ}, so \\vec{ST} is a scalar multiple of \\vec{PQ} and ST is parallel to PQ. In the quadrilateral PQTS the sides PQ and TS are parallel, but QT and SP are not, so exactly one pair of opposite sides is parallel and PQTS is a trapezium.","solution":"From (a) (i), \\vec{PQ} = q - p, and from (b), \\vec{ST} = (1/2)(q - p). Hence \\vec{ST} = (1/2)\\vec{PQ}. One vector is a scalar multiple of the other, so ST is parallel to PQ and half its length. In PQTS the sides PQ and TS are therefore parallel, while \\vec{QT} = -(1/2)q and \\vec{SP} = (1/2)p are not parallel, because p and q are not parallel. A quadrilateral with exactly one pair of parallel sides is a trapezium.","criteria":[{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"shows that \\vec{ST} is (1/2)\\vec{PQ}, a scalar multiple of it","check":{"type":"written","id":"multiple","description":"shows that \\vec{ST} is (1/2)\\vec{PQ}, a scalar multiple of it","any":["scalar multiple","multiple of","1/2","half","0.5"]},"field":"answer","code":"B1"},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"states that ST is parallel to PQ","check":{"type":"written","id":"parallel","description":"states that ST is parallel to PQ","any":["parallel","same direction","same gradient"]},"field":"answer","code":"B2"},{"kind":"B","marks":1,"description":"names PQTS as a trapezium","check":{"type":"written","id":"trapezium","description":"names PQTS as a trapezium","any":["trapezium","trapezoid"]},"field":"answer","code":"B3"}]}},{"id":"p2h-q10::d","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"p2h-q10::d","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"math-paper2","sourceMarking":{"answer":"sqrt(13)","solution":"\\vec{ST} = (1/2)(q - p) = (1/2)[[6], [4]] = [[3], [2]]. So |\\vec{ST}| = sqrt((3)^2 + (2)^2) = sqrt(9 + 4) = sqrt(13), which is 3.61 correct to 2 decimal places.","criteria":[{"kind":"M","marks":1,"description":"uses |v| = sqrt(x^2 + y^2)","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"contains","value":[13]},{"type":"contains","value":[9,4]}]},"field":"all","code":"M1"},{"kind":"A","marks":1,"description":"the magnitude of \\vec{ST}","check":{"type":"anyOf","options":[{"type":"expression","value":"sqrt(13)","accepted":["3.61"]},{"type":"numeric","value":3.605551275463989,"tolerance":0.01}]},"field":"answer","depends":[],"code":"A1"}]}}]'::jsonb,false,'draft')
