sted strategies are likely to be successful."],"guide":["Use complete paragraphs rather than a list.","Develop explanations by linking cause, action and effect.","Use relevant Caribbean examples.","Keep the response organised around the tasks in the question."],"component":"content"}},{"id":"ss-p2-q5::organisation","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"ss-p2-q5::organisation","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"social-studies-essay","sourceMarking":{"tasks":["Identify TWO agents that transmit Caribbean culture.","State TWO examples of Caribbean cultural forms that have reached audiences outside the region.","Explain TWO ways cultural transmission may strengthen Caribbean identity.","Suggest THREE strategies that cultural organisations could use to preserve and promote Caribbean cultural forms.","Explain why any TWO of the suggested strategies are likely to be successful."],"component":"organisation"}},{"id":"ss-p2-q6::content","maxMarks":18,"sourcePartId":"ss-p2-q6::content","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"social-studies-essay","sourceMarking":{"tasks":["State TWO reasons Caribbean countries pursue regional integration.","Identify TWO regional institutions or arrangements that support cooperation.","Explain TWO benefits regional integration may bring to Caribbean development.","Suggest THREE actions governments, businesses or citizens could take to strengthen regional cooperation.","Explain why any TWO of the suggested actions are likely to be successful."],"guide":["Answer in essay format.","Use accurate regional examples where relevant.","Separate benefits from actions and explain each point fully.","Allow time to plan, organise and check the response."],"component":"content"}},{"id":"ss-p2-q6::organisation","maxMarks":4,"sourcePartId":"ss-p2-q6::organisation","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"social-studies-essay","sourceMarking":{"tasks":["State TWO reasons Caribbean countries pursue regional integratio