itched on."],"guidance":"1 mark for a clearly stated hypothesis; 1 mark for a testable hypothesis","alternatives":null},"profile":{"XS":2},"requiredResponseType":"lines"}},{"id":"IS-M1-P2-05::(b)::(ii)","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"IS-M1-P2-05::(b)::(ii)","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"integrated-science-paper2","sourceMarking":{"markScheme":{"points":["Manipulated: presence/absence (or speed) of wind from the fan (1)","Responding: distance moved by the air bubble in a fixed time / rate of water uptake (1)"],"guidance":"1 mark each","alternatives":null},"profile":{"XS":2},"requiredResponseType":"lines"}},{"id":"IS-M1-P2-05::(b)::(iii)","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"IS-M1-P2-05::(b)::(iii)","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"integrated-science-paper2","sourceMarking":{"markScheme":{"points":["Cut the shoot under water to prevent air entering the xylem","Make sure the apparatus is airtight (seal joints with Vaseline)","Keep light and temperature the same","Repeat readings and find an average"],"guidance":"Any one, 1 mark","alternatives":null},"profile":{"XS":1},"requiredResponseType":"lines"}},{"id":"IS-M1-P2-05::(b)::(iv)","maxMarks":2,"sourcePartId":"IS-M1-P2-05::(b)::(iv)","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"integrated-science-paper2","sourceMarking":{"markScheme":{"points":["The bubble would move more slowly (1)","because the air inside the bag becomes humid, reducing the concentration gradient of water vapour, so less water evaporates from the leaves (1)"],"guidance":"1 mark for prediction; 1 mark for explanation","alternatives":null},"profile":{"UK":2},"requiredResponseType":"lines"}},{"id":"IS-M1-P2-05::(c)::(i)","maxMarks":1,"sourcePartId":"IS-M1-P2-05::(c)::(i)","kind":"structured","acceptedPhrases":[],"sourceFormat":"integrated-science-paper2","sourceMarking":{"markScheme":{"points":["Xylem"],"guidance":"1 mark","alternatives":null},"profile":{"KC":1},"requiredResponseType":"lines"}},{"id":"